INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Ring Dips', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Grip a ring in each hand, and then take a small jump to help you get into the position de depart with vos bras locked out. 2. Begin by flexing the coudes, lowering votre corps until vos bras break 90 degrees. Avoid swinging, and maintain good posture throughout the descent. 3. Reverse the motion by extending the coudes, pushing yourself back up into the position de depart. 4. Repetez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Ring_Dips/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rocket Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a relaxed stance with vos pieds epaules width apart and hold vos bras close to the body. 2. To initiate the move, squat down halfway and explode back up as high as possible. 3. Fully extend your entire body, reaching overhead as far as possible. As you land, absorb your impact through the legs.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rocket_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rocking Standing Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place it on the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck). 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance. Also maintain a straight back and keep the genoux with a slight bend; never locked. Position de depart. 4. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your ankles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genoux is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending (other than the slight initial bend we created during positioning) at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down. 5. Go back Lentement, to the position de depart as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the ankles until mollets are stretched. 6. Now lift your toes by contracting the tibia muscles in the front of the mollets as you Expirez. 7. Maintenez 1 seconde and bring them back down as you Inspirez. 8. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rocking_Standing_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rocky Pull-Ups/Pulldowns', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the palms facing forward using a prise large. 2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. Position de depart. 3. Pull your torse up until the bar touches your upper poitrine by drawing the epaules and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar. 4. After a second on the contracted position, start to inhale and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de depart when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. 5. Now Repetez the same movements as described above except this time your torse will remain straight as you go up and the bar will touch the back of the neck instead of the upper poitrine. Conseil : Use the head to lean forward slightly as it will help you properly execute this portion of the exercise. 6. Once you have lowered yourself back down to the position de depart, Repetez the exercise for the prescribed amount of repetitions in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rocky_Pull-Ups_Pulldowns/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Romanian Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Put a barre in front of you on the ground and grab it using a pronated (palms facing down) grip that a little wider than epaules width. Conseil : Depending on the poids used, you may need poignets wraps to perform the exercise and also a raised platform in order to allow for better range of motion. 2. Bend the genoux slightly and keep the shins vertical, hips back and back straight. Position de depart. 3. Keeping votre dos and arms completely straight en permanence, use your hips to lift the bar en expirant. Conseil : le mouvement should not be fast but steady and under control. 4. Once you are standing completely straight up, lower the bar by pushing the hips back, only slightly bending the genoux, unlike when squatting. Conseil : Take a deep breath at the start of le mouvement and keep your poitrine up. Hold your breath as you lower and exhale as you complete le mouvement. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Romanian_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Romanian Deadlift from Deficit', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin standing while holding a bar at arm''s length in front of you. You can stand on a raised platform to increase the range of motion. 2. Begin by flexing the genoux slightly, and then flex at the hip, moving your butt back as far as possible, lowering the torse as far as flexibility allows. The back should remain in absolute extension en permanence, and the bar should remain in contact with the legs. If done properly, there should be heavy tension felt in the ischio-jambiers. 3. Reverse the motion to Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Romanian_Deadlift_from_Deficit/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Climb', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grab the rope with both hands above your head. Pull down on the rope as you take a small jump. 2. Wrap the rope around one leg, using vos pieds to pinch the rope. Reach up as high as possible with vos bras, gripping the rope tightly. 3. Release the rope from vos pieds as you pull yourself up with vos bras, bringing your genoux towards your poitrine. 4. Resecure vos pieds on the rope, and then stand up to take another high hold on the rope. Continue until you reach the top of the rope. 5. To lower yourself, loosen the grip of vos pieds on the rope as you slide down using a hand over hand motion.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Avant-bras, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Climb/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Kneel 1-2 feet in front of a cable system with a rope attached. 2. After selecting an appropriate poids, grasp the rope with both hands reaching overhead. Your torse should be upright in the position de depart. 3. To begin, flex at the spine, attempting to bring your rib cage to vos jambes as you pull the cable down. 4. Pause at the bottom of the motion, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de depart. 5. These can be done with twists or to the side to hit the obliques.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Jumping', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Hold an end of the rope in each hand. Position the rope behind you on the ground. Raise vos bras up and turn the rope over your head bringing it down in front of you. When it reaches the ground, jump over it. Find a good turning pace that can be maintained. Different speeds and techniques can be used to introduce variation. 2. Rope jumping is exciting, challenges your coordination, and requires a lot of energy. A 150 lb person will burn about 350 calories jumping rope for 30 minutes, compared to over 450 calories running.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Jumping/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rope Straight-Arm Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to a high pulley and make your poids selection. Stand a couple feet back from the pulley with vos pieds staggered and take the rope with both hands. Lean forward from the hip, keeping votre dos straight, with vos bras extended up in front of you. Position de depart. 2. Keeping vos bras straight, extend the epaules to pull the rope down to your cuisses. 3. Pause at the bottom of the motion, squeezing your lats. 4. Revenez en position de depart without allowing the poids to fully rest on the stack.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rope_Straight-Arm_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Round The World Shoulder Stretch', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos jambes together, holding a bodybar or broomstick. 2. Hold the pole behind your hips with a wider than epaules width grip. Your palms should be down and your thumbs facing out. 3. Lentement, lift vos bras up behind your head. Don''t force it if it gets hard to lift further.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Pectoraux. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Round_The_World_Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Rowing, Stationary', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, seat yourself on the rower. Make sure that your heels are resting comfortably against the base of the foot pedals and that the straps are secured. Select the program that you wish to use, if applicable. Sit up straight and bend forward at the hips. 2. There are three phases of movement when using a rower. The first phase is when you come forward on the rower. Your genoux are bent and against your poitrine. Your upper body is leaning slightly forward while still maintaining good posture. Next, push against the foot pedals and extend vos jambes while bringing vos mains to your upper abdominal area, squeezing your epaules back as you do so. To avoid straining votre dos, use primarily your leg and hip muscles. 3. The recovery phase simply involves straightening vos bras, bending the genoux, and bringing votre corps forward again as you transition back into the first phase.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Rowing_Stationary/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Runner''s Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. It''s easiest to get into this stretch if you start standing up, put one leg behind you, and Lentement, lower your torse down to le sol. 2. Keep the front heel on le sol (if it lifts up, scoot your other leg further back). 3. Place vos mains on either side of your front leg. To get more out of this stretch, push your butt up toward the ceiling, and then gradually lower it back toward le sol. You''ll Stretch the hip flexor of the back leg and the ischio-jambiers and buttocks of the front.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Runners_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Running, Treadmill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the treadmill and select the desired option from the menu. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout. 2. Treadmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than running outside. A 150 lb person will burn over 450 calories running 8 miles per hour for 30 minutes. Maintain proper posture as you run, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Running_Treadmill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Russian Twist', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol placing vos pieds either under something that will not move or by having a partner hold them. vos jambes should be bent at the genoux. 2. Elevate your upper body so that it creates an imaginary V-shape with your cuisses. vos bras should be fully extended in front of you perpendicular to your torse and with the hands clasped. Position de depart. 3. Twist your torse to the right side until vos bras are parallel with le sol while breathing out. 4. Hold the contraction for a second and move back to the position de depart while breathing out. Now move to the opposite side performing the same techniques you applied to the right side. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Russian_Twist/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sandbag Load', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. To load sandbags or other objects, begin with the implements placed a distance from the loading platform, typically 50 feet. 2. Begin by lifting the sandbag. Sandbags are extremely awkward, and the manner of lifting them can vary depending on the particular sandbag used. Reach as far around it as possible, extending through the hips and genoux to pull it up high. Shouldering is usually not allowed. 3. Move as quickly as possible to the platform, and load it, extending through your hips, genoux, and ankles to get it as high as possible. Place it onto the platform, ensuring it doesn''t fall off. 4. Revenez en position de depart to retrieve the next sandbag, and Repetez until the event is completed.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Biceps, Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sandbag_Load/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Scapular Pull-Up', 'Trapèzes', 'Autre', '1. Take a pronated grip on a pull-up bar. 2. From a hanging position, raise yourself a few inches without using vos bras. Do this by depressing your epaules girdle in a reverse shrugging motion. 3. Pause at the completion of le mouvement, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de depart before performing more repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Scapular_Pull-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Scissor Kick', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, lie down with votre dos pressed against le sol or on an exercise mat (optional). vos bras should be fully extended to the sides with your palms facing down. Note: The arms should be stationary the entire time. 2. With a slight bend at the genoux, lift vos jambes up so that your heels are about 6 inches off the ground. Position de depart. 3. Now lift your left leg up to about a 45 degree angle while your right leg is lowered until the heel is about 2-3 inches from the ground. 4. Switch movements by raising your right leg up and lowering your left leg. Remember to breathe while performing this exercise. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Scissor_Kick/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Scissors Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Assume a lunge stance position with one foot forward with the genoux bent, and the rear genoux nearly touching the ground. 2. Ensure that the front genoux is over the midline of the foot. Extending through both legs, jump as high as possible, swinging vos bras to gain lift. 3. As you jump as high as you can, switch the position of vos jambes, moving your front leg to the back and the rear leg to the front. 4. As you land, absorb the impact through the legs by adopting the lunge position, and Repetez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Scissors_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Band Hamstring Curl', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Secure a band close to the ground and place a banc a couple feet away from it. 2. Seat yourself on the banc and secure the band behind your ankles, beginning with vos jambes straight. Position de depart. 3. Flex the genoux, bringing vos pieds towards the banc. You may need to lean back slightly to keep vos pieds from striking le sol. 4. Pause at the completion of le mouvement, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de depart.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Band_Hamstring_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Barbell Military Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Sit on a Military Press banc with a bar behind your head and either have a spotter give you the bar (better on the rotator cuff this way) or pick it up yourself carefully with a pronated grip (palms facing forward). Conseil : Your grip should be wider than epaules width and it should create a 90-degree angle between the forearm and the upper arm as the barre goes down. 2. Once you pick up the barre with the correct grip length, lift the bar up over your head by locking vos bras. Hold at about epaules level and slightly in front of your head. Position de depart. 3. Lower the bar down to the collarbone Lentement, en inspirant. 4. Lift the bar back up to the position de depart en expirant. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Barbell_Military_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Barbell Twist', 'Abdominaux', 'Barre', '1. Start out by sitting at the end of a flat banc with a barre placed on top of your cuisses. vos pieds should be epaules width apart from each other. 2. Grip the bar with your palms facing down and make sure vos mains are wider than epaules width apart from each other. Begin to lift the barre up over your head until vos bras are fully extended. 3. Now lower the barre behind your head until it is resting along the base of your neck. Position de depart. 4. While keeping vos pieds and head stationary, move your waist from side to side so that your oblique muscles feel the contraction. Only move from side to side as far as your waist will allow you to go. Stretching or moving too far can cause an injury to occur. Conseil : Use a slow and controlled motion. 5. Remember to Expirez while twisting votre corps to the side and in when moving back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Barbell_Twist/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit down at the end of a flat banc with a halteres in one arm using a neutral grip (palms of the hand facing you). 2. Bend your genoux slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to le sol. Make sure that you keep the head up. 3. The upper arm with the halteres should be close to the torse and aligned with it (lifted up until it is parallel to le sol while the forearms are pointing towards le sol as the hands hold the poids). Conseil : There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearms and the upper arm. Position de depart. 4. Keeping the upper arm stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids en expirant until the forearm is parallel to le sol and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves. 5. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the halteres back to the position de depart en inspirant. 6. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions. 7. Switch arms and Repetez the exercise.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Bent-Over Rear Delt Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Place a couple of halteres looking forward in front of a flat banc. 2. Sit on the end of the banc with vos jambes together and the halteres behind your mollets. 3. Bend at the waist while keeping the back straight in order to pick up the halteres. The palms of vos mains should be facing each other as you pick them. Position de depart. 4. Keeping your torse forward and stationary, and the arms slightly bent at the coudes, lift the halteres straight to the side until both arms are parallel to le sol. Exhale as you lift the poids. (Note: avoid swinging the torse or bringing the arms back as opposed to the side.) 5. After a one second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the halteres back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_Rear_Delt_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit down at the end of a flat banc with a halteres in both arms using a neutral grip (palms of the hand facing you). 2. Bend your genoux slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to le sol. Make sure that you keep the head up. 3. The upper arms with the halteres should be close to the torse and aligned with it (lifted up until they are parallel to le sol while the forearms are pointing towards le sol as the hands hold the poids). Conseil : There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearms and the upper arm. Position de depart. 4. Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids en expirant until the forearms are parallel to le sol and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves. 5. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the halteres back to the position de depart en inspirant. 6. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Bent-Over_Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Biceps', 'Biceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Sit on le sol with your genoux bent and your partner standing behind you. Extend vos bras straight behind you with your palms facing each other. Your partner will hold your poignets for you. This will be the position de depart. 2. Attempt to flex your coudes, while your partner prevents any actual movement. 3. After 10-20 seconds, relax vos bras while your partner gently pulls your poignets up to stretch your biceps. Be sure to let your partner know when the stretch is appropriate to prevent injury or overstretching.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Biceps/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Cable Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Poulie', '1. For this exercise you will need access to a low pulley row machine with a V-bar. Note: The V-bar will enable you to have a neutral grip where the palms of vos mains face each other. To get into the position de depart, first sit down on the machine and place vos pieds on the front platform or crossbar provided making sure that your genoux are slightly bent and not locked. 2. Lean over as you keep the natural alignment of votre dos and grab the V-bar handles. 3. With vos bras extended pull back until your torse is at a 90-degree angle from vos jambes. votre dos should be slightly arched and your poitrine should be sticking out. You should be feeling a nice stretch on your lats as you hold the bar in front of you. Position de depart. of the exercise. 4. Keeping the torse stationary, pull the handles back towards your torse while keeping the arms close to it until you touch the abdominals. Expirez as you perform that movement. At that point you should be squeezing votre dos muscles hard. Hold that contraction for a second and Lentement, go back to the original position while breathing in. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Cable_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Cable Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Adjust the poids to an appropriate amount and be seated, grasping the handles. Your upper arms should be about 90 degrees to the body, with your head and poitrine up. The coudes should also be bent to about 90 degrees. Position de depart. 2. Begin by extending through the coudes, pressing the handles together above your head. 3. After pausing at the top, return the handles to the position de depart. Ensure that you maintain tension on the cables. 4. You can also execute this movement with votre dos off the pad and alternate hands.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Cable_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Sit on the machine and place your toes on the lower portion of the platform provided with the heels extending off. Choose the toe positioning of your choice (forward, in, or out) as per the beginning of this chapter. 2. Place your lower cuisses under the lever pad, which will need to be adjusted according to the height of your cuisses. Now place vos mains on top of the lever pad in order to prevent it from slipping forward. 3. Lift the lever slightly by pushing your heels up and release the safety bar. Position de depart. 4. Lentement, lower your heels by bending at the ankles until the mollets are fully stretched. Inhale as you perform this movement. 5. Raise the heels by extending the ankles as high as possible as you contract the mollets and Expirez. Hold the top contraction for a second. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Calf Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Sit up straight on an exercise mat. 2. Bend one genoux and put that foot on le sol to stabilize the torse. 3. Straighten your other leg and flex your ankle. 4. Using a band, towel, or your hand if you can reach, pull the toes toward you. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Close-Grip Concentration Barbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Sit down on a flat banc with a barre or E-Z Bar in front of you in between vos jambes. vos jambes should be spread with the genoux bent and the feet on le sol. 2. Use vos bras to pick the barre up and place the back of your upper arms on top of your inner cuisses (around three and a half inches away from the front of the genoux). A supinated grip closer than epaules width is needed to perform this exercise. Conseil : Your arm should be extended bras tendus and the barre should be above le sol. Position de depart. 3. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. 4. Lentement, begin to bring the barre back to position de depart as your Inspirez. Conseil : Avoid swinging motions at any time. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Close-Grip_Concentration_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on a flat banc with a halteres on each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse. 2. Rotate the palms of the hands so that they are facing your torse. Position de depart. 3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the poids and start twisting the poignets once the halteres pass your cuisses so that the palms of vos mains face forward at the end of le mouvement. Make sure that you contract the biceps as you Expirez and make sure that only the forearms move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. 4. Lentement, begin to bring the halteres back to the position de depart as your Inspirez and as you rotate the poignets back to a neutral grip. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Inner Biceps Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on the end of a flat banc with a halteres in each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse. 2. Rotate the palms of the hands so that they are facing inward in a neutral position. Position de depart. 3. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the halteres out and up, turning the palms out as you lift and keeping your forearms in line with your outer deltoids. Tips: 4. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. 5. Lentement, begin to bring the halteres back to the position de depart as your Inspirez. Remember to rotate vos bras as you lower the halteres so that you can switch back to a neutral grip. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Inner_Biceps_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Palms-Down Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Start out by placing two halteres on le sol in front of a flat banc. 2. Sit down on the edge of the flat banc with vos jambes at about epaules width apart. Make sure to keep vos pieds on le sol. 3. Use vos bras to grab both of the halteres and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against your cuisses with the palms of the hands facing down. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge of your cuisses. 4. Start out by curling your poignets upwards and exhaling. 5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de depart while inhaling. Make sure to inhale during this part of the exercise. Conseil : Your forearms should be stationary as your poignets is the only movement needed to perform this exercise. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 7. When finished, simply lower the halteres to le sol.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Palms-Up Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Start out by placing two halteres on le sol in front of a flat banc. 2. Sit down on the edge of the flat banc with vos jambes at about epaules width apart. Make sure to keep vos pieds on le sol. 3. Use vos bras to grab both of the halteres and bring them up so that your forearms are resting against your cuisses with the palms of the hands facing up. Your poignets should be hanging over the edge of your cuisses. 4. Start out by curling your poignets upwards and exhaling. 5. Lentement, lower your poignets back down to the position de depart while inhaling. Make sure to inhale during this part of the exercise. Conseil : Your forearms should be stationary as your poignets is the only movement needed to perform this exercise. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 7. When finished, simply lower the halteres to le sol.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Palms-Up_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a couple of halteres and sit on a military press banc or a utility banc that has a back support on it as you place the halteres upright on top of your cuisses. 2. Clean the halteres up one at a time by using your cuisses to bring the halteres up to epaules height at each side. 3. Rotate the poignets so that the palms of vos mains are facing forward. Position de depart. 4. en expirant, push the halteres up until they touch at the top. 5. Apres une pause, Lentement, come down back to the position de depart en inspirant. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Flat Bench Leg Pull-In', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with the legs stretched out in front of you slightly below parallel and vos bras holding on to the sides of the banc. Your torse should be leaning backwards around a 45-degree angle from the banc. Position de depart. 2. Bring the genoux in toward you as you move your torse closer to them at the same time. Expirez as you perform this movement. 3. Apres une pause, go back to the position de depart en inspirant. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Flat_Bench_Leg_Pull-In/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Floor Hamstring Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Sit on a mat with your right leg extended in front of you and your left leg bent with your foot against your right inner cuisses. 2. Lean forward from your hips and reach for your ankle until you feel a stretch in your ischio-jambiers. Hold for 15 seconds, then Repetez for your other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Floor_Hamstring_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Front Deltoid', 'Épaules', 'Poids de corps', '1. Sit upright on le sol with vos jambes bent, your partner standing behind you. Stick vos bras straight out to your sides, with your palms facing the ground. Attempt to move them as far behind you as possible, as your assistant holds your poignets. Position de depart. 2. Keeping your coudes straight, attempt to move vos bras to the front, with your partner gently restraining you to prevent any actual movement for 10-20 seconds. 3. Now, relax your muscles and allow your partner to gently increase the stretch on the epaules and poitrine. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Front_Deltoid/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Glute', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. In a seated position with your genoux bent, cross one ankle over the opposite genoux. Your partner will stand behind you. Now, lean forward as your partner braces your epaules with their hands. Position de depart. 2. Attempt to push your torse back for 10-20 seconds, as your partner prevents any actual movement of your torse. 3. Now relax your muscles as your partner increases the stretch by gently pushing your torse forward for 10-20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Glute/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Good Mornings', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. Set up a box in a power rack. The pins should be set at an appropriate height. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the epaules, not on top of your traps. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your epaules. 2. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back. Keep your head facing forward. With votre dos, epaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genoux and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the bar tight, bend forward at the hips as much as possible. If you set the pins to what would be parallel, you not only have a safety if you fail, but know when to stop. 4. Pause just above the pins and reverse the motion until your torse it upright.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Good_Mornings/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Hamstring', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. In a seated position with vos jambes extended, have your partner stand behind you. Now, lean forward as your partner braces your epaules with their hands. Position de depart. 2. Attempt to push your torse back for 10-20 seconds, as your partner prevents any actual movement of your torse. 3. Now relax your muscles as your partner increases the stretch by gently pushing your torse forward for 10-20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Hamstring/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Hamstring and Calf Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Loop a belt, rope, or band around one foot. Sit down with both legs extended . Position de depart. 2. Leaning forward slightly, pull on the belt to draw the toes of your foot back. Hold this position for 10-20 seconds and then Repetez with the other leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Hamstring_and_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Head Harness Neck Resistance', 'Cou', 'Autre', '1. Place a neck strap on le sol at the end of a flat banc. Once you have selected the poids, sit at the end of the flat banc with vos pieds wider than epaules width apart from each other. Your toes should be pointed out. 2. Lentement, move your torse forward until it is almost parallel with le sol. Using both hands, securely position the neck strap around your head. Conseil : Make sure the poids are still lying on le sol to prevent any strain on the neck. Now grab the poids with both hands while elevating your torse back until it is almost perpendicular to le sol. Note: Your head and torse needs to be slightly tilted forward to perform this exercise. 3. Now place both hands on top of your genoux. Position de depart. 4. Lentement, lower your neck down until your chin touches the upper part of your poitrine while breathing in. 5. While exhaling, bring your neck back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Head_Harness_Neck_Resistance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Leg Curl', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the machine lever to fit your height and sit on the machine with votre dos against the back support pad. 2. Place the back of lower leg on top of padded lever (just a few inches under the mollets) and secure the lap pad against your cuisses, just above the genoux. Then grasp the side handles on the machine as you point your toes straight (or you can also use any of the other two stances) and ensure that the legs are fully straight right in front of you. Position de depart. 3. en expirant, pull the machine lever as far as possible to the back of your cuisses by flexing at the genoux. Keep your torse stationary en permanence. Maintenez 1 seconde. 4. Lentement, Revenez en position de depart as you Inspirez. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Leg_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Leg Tucks', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with the legs stretched out in front of you slightly below parallel and vos bras holding on to the sides of the banc. Your torse should be leaning backwards around a 45-degree angle from the banc. Position de depart. 2. Bring the genoux in toward you as you move your torse closer to them at the same time. Expirez as you perform this movement. 3. Apres une pause, go back to the position de depart en inspirant. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Leg_Tucks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Down Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on a flat banc with a halteres in your right hand. 2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than epaules width apart. 3. Lean forward and place your right forearm on top of your upper right cuisses with your palm down. Conseil : Make sure that the back of the poignets lies on top of your genoux. Position de depart. 4. Lower the halteres as far as possible as you keep a tight grip on the halteres. Inhale as you perform this movement. 5. Now curl the halteres as high as possible as you contract the forearms and en expirant. Keep the contraction for a second before you lower again. Conseil : The only movement should happen at the poignets. 6. Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch arms and Repetez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Palms-Down_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated One-Arm Dumbbell Palms-Up Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Haltères', '1. Sit on a flat banc with a halteres in your right hand. 2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than epaules width apart. 3. Lean forward and place your right forearm on top of your upper right cuisses with your palm up. Conseil : Make sure that the front of the poignets lies on top of your genoux. Position de depart. 4. Lower the halteres as far as possible as you keep a tight grip on the halteres. Inhale as you perform this movement. 5. Now curl the halteres as high as possible as you contract the forearms and en expirant. Keep the contraction for a second before you lower again. Conseil : The only movement should happen at the poignets. 6. Perform for the recommended amount of repetitions, switch arms and Repetez le mouvement.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Palms-Up_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated One-arm Cable Pulley Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Poulie', '1. To get into the position de depart, first sit down on the machine and place vos pieds on the front platform or crossbar provided making sure that your genoux are slightly bent and not locked. 2. Lean over as you keep the natural alignment of votre dos and grab the single handle attachment with your left arm using a palms-down grip. 3. With your arm extended pull back until your torse is at a 90-degree angle from vos jambes. votre dos should be slightly arched and your poitrine should be sticking out. You should be feeling a nice stretch on your lat as you hold the bar in front of you. The right arm can be kept by the waist. Position de depart. of the exercise. 4. Keeping the torse stationary, pull the handles back towards your torse while keeping the arms close to it as you rotate the poignets, so that by the time your hand is by your abdominals it is in a neutral position (palms facing the torse). Expirez as you perform that movement. At that point you should be squeezing votre dos muscles hard. 5. Hold that contraction for a second and Lentement, go back to the original position while breathing in. Conseil : Remember to rotate the poignets as you go back to the position de depart so that the palms are facing down again. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. and then perform the same movement with the right hand.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_One-arm_Cable_Pulley_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Overhead Stretch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Sit up straight on an exercise mat. 2. Touch the soles of vos pieds together with vos pieds six to eight inches in front of your hips. 3. Place one hand on le sol beside you and your other hand behind your head. 4. Lift your coudes to the ceiling as you incline your torse to the other side. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Overhead_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Palm-Up Barbell Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your palms facing up; hands spaced about epaules width. 2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than epaules width apart. 3. Lean forward and place your forearms on top of your upper cuisses with your palms up. Conseil : Make sure that the front of the poignets lay on top of your genoux. Position de depart. 4. Lower the bar as far as possible while inhaling and keeping a tight grip. 5. Now curl bar up as high as possible while flexing the forearms and exhaling. Hold the contraction at the top for a second and Conseil : Only the poignets should move.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Palm-Up_Barbell_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Palms-Down Barbell Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your palms facing down; hands spaced about epaules width. 2. Place vos pieds flat on le sol, at a distance that is slightly wider than epaules width apart. 3. Lean forward and place your forearms on top of your upper cuisses with your palms down. Conseil : Make sure that the back of the poignets lay on top of your genoux. Position de depart. 4. Lower the bar as far as possible while inhaling and keeping a tight grip. 5. Now curl bar up as high as possible while flexing the forearms and exhaling. Hold the contraction at the top for a second and Conseil : Only the poignets should move.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Palms-Down_Barbell_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Side Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Pick a couple of halteres and sit at the end of a flat banc with vos pieds firmly on le sol. Hold the halteres with your palms facing in and vos bras straight down at your sides at arms'' length. Position de depart. 2. While maintaining the torse stationary (no swinging), lift the halteres to your side with a slight bend on the coudes and the hands slightly tilted forward as if pouring water in a glass. Continue to go up until you arms are parallel to le sol. Exhale as you execute this movement and pause for a second at the top. 3. Lower the halteres back down Lentement, to the position de depart en inspirant. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Side_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Triceps Press', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Asseyez-vous sur un banc with back support and grasp a halteres with both hands and hold it overhead at arm''s length. Conseil : a better way is to have somebody hand it to you especially if it is very heavy. The resistance should be resting in the palms of vos mains with your thumbs around it. The palm of the hand should be facing inward. Position de depart. 2. Keeping your upper arms close to your head (coudes in) and perpendicular to le sol, lower the resistance in a semi-circular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step. 3. Go back to the position de depart by using the triceps to raise the halteres. Expirez as you perform this step. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Triceps_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Seated Two-Arm Palms-Up Low-Pulley Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Poulie', '1. Put a banc in front of a low pulley machine that has a barre or EZ Curl attachment on it. 2. Move the banc far enough away so that when you bring the handle to the top of your cuisses tension is created on the cable due to the poids stack being moved up. 3. Now hold the handle with both hands, palms up, using a epaules-width grip. 4. Step back and sit on the banc with vos pieds about epaules width apart, firmly on le sol. 5. Lean forward and place the forearms on your cuisses with the back of your poignets over your genoux. Position de depart. 6. Lower the bar as far as possible, while inhaling and keeping a tight grip. 7. Now curl the bar up as high as possible while contracting the forearms. Conseil : Only the poignets should move; not the forearms. 8. After a second contraction at the top go back to the position de depart en inspirant. 9. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Seated_Two-Arm_Palms-Up_Low-Pulley_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('See-Saw Press (Alternating Side Press)', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a halteres with each hand and stand up erect. 2. Clean (lift) the halteres to the poitrine/epaules level and then rotate your poignets so that your palms are facing towards you as if you were getting ready to perform an Arnold Press. Position de depart. 3. Now start extending your left arm overhead as you rotate the poignets so that the palm of your hand faces forward as you go up. Your coudes should come out also as you lift the poids. Simultaneously, you will also be bending from your hip to your opposite side. Conseil : If you perform the exercise correctly, is should look as if you are trying to reach for something overhead on the right hand side of votre corps, but with your left arm. Expirez as you perform this movement. 4. Once you reach the top position Inspirez. Then, with the poids fully extended overhead and you bent over to your right hand side, begin le mouvement to the left side. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/See-Saw_Press_Alternating_Side_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Shotgun Row', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a single handle to a low cable. 2. After selecting the correct poids, stand a couple feet back with a wide-split stance. Your arm should be extended and your epaules forward. Position de depart. 3. Perform le mouvement by retracting the epaules and flexing the coudes. As you pull, supinate the poignets, turning the palm upward as you go. 4. Apres une pause, Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Shotgun_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Shoulder Circles', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. With epaules relaxed and arms resting loosely at your sides (or in your lap if you''re seated), gently roll your epaules forward, up, back, and down. 2. Reverse direction. You can do this exercise alternating epaules or both at the same time.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Shoulder_Circles/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Shoulder Press - With Bands', 'Épaules', 'Élastique', '1. To begin, stand on an exercise band so that tension begins at arm''s length. Grasp the handles and lift them so that the hands are at epaules height at each side. 2. Rotate the poignets so that the palms of vos mains are facing forward. Your coudes should be bent, with the upper arms and forearms in line to the torse. Position de depart. 3. en expirant, lift the handles up until vos bras are fully extended overhead.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Shoulder_Press_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Shoulder Raise', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Relax vos bras to your sides and raise your epaules up toward your ears, then back down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Shoulder Stretch', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Reach your left arm across votre corps and hold it straight.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Shoulder_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side-Lying Floor Stretch', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. First lie on your left side, bending your left genoux in front of you to stabilize your torse (use your abdominal muscles as well to hold you upright). 2. Straighten your right leg and rest the right foot on le sol behind your left. Straighten your right arm over your head and gently pull on your right poignets to stretch the entire right side of the body. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side-Lying_Floor_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Bridge', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Bridge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Hop-Sprint', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand to the side of a cone or hurdle. 2. Begin this drill by hopping sideways over the obstacle, rebounding out of your landing to hop back to where you started. 3. Hop for a prescribed number or repetitions as quickly as possible, and finish this drill by sprinting a short distance upon landing the last hop.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Hop-Sprint/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Jackknife', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Jackknife/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Lateral Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Pick a couple of halteres and Tenez-vous debout avec a straight torse and the halteres by your side bras tendus with the palms of the hand facing you. Position de depart. 2. While maintaining the torse in a stationary position (no swinging), lift the halteres to your side with a slight bend on the coudes and the hands slightly tilted forward as if pouring water in a glass. Continue to go up until you arms are parallel to le sol. Exhale as you execute this movement and pause for a second at the top. 3. Lower the halteres back down Lentement, to the position de depart en inspirant. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Lateral_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Laterals to Front Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. In a standing position, hold a pair of halteres at your side. Position de depart. 2. Keeping your coudes slightly bent, raise the poids directly in front of you to epaules height, avoiding any swinging or cheating. 3. At the top of the exercise move the poids out in front of you, keeping vos bras extended. 4. Lower the poids with a controlled motion. 5. On the next repetition, raise the poids in front of you to epaules height before moving the poids laterally to your sides. 6. Lower the poids to the position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Laterals_to_Front_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Leg Raises', 'Adducteurs', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand next to a chair, which you may hold onto as a support. Stand on one leg. Position de depart. 2. Keeping your leg straight, raise it as far out to the side as possible, and swing it back down, allowing it to cross the opposite leg. 3. Repetez this swinging motion 5-10 times, increasing the range of motion as you do so.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Leg_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Lying Groin Stretch', 'Adducteurs', 'Autre', '1. Start off by lying on your right side and bend your right genoux in front of you to stabilize the torse. 2. Rest your head on your right hand or epaules. Lift your left leg upward and hold it by the back of the genoux (easier) or the foot (harder). 3. Pull your left genoux in toward your left epaules and simultaneously press your foot or genoux down to le sol. To intensify this stretch, straighten your left leg. Switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Lying_Groin_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Neck Stretch', 'Cou', 'Autre', '1. Start with your epaules relaxed, gently tilt your head towards your epaules. 2. Assist stretch with a gentle pull on the side of the head.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Neck_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Standing Long Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Begin standing with vos pieds hip width apart in an athletic stance. Your head and poitrine should be up, genoux and hips slightly bent. Position de depart. 2. Leaning to your right, extend through your hips, genoux, and ankles to jump into the air. Block with the arms to lead le mouvement, jumping as far to your right as you can. 3. Land facing the same direction with vos pieds hip width apart, absorbing the impact through your lower body.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Standing_Long_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side To Side Chins', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the palms facing forward using a prise large. 2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at a prise large, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. Position de depart. 3. Pull your torse up while leaning to the left hand side until the bar almost touches your upper poitrine by drawing the epaules and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space (no swinging) and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar. 4. After a second of contraction, inhale as you go back to the position de depart. 5. Now, pull your torse up while leaning to the right hand side until the bar almost touches your upper poitrine by drawing the epaules and the upper arms down and back. Exhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar. 6. After a second of contraction, inhale as you go back to the position de depart. 7. Repetez steps 3-6 until you have performed the prescribed amount of repetitions for each side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Avant-bras, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_To_Side_Chins/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side Wrist Pull', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. This stretch works best standing. Cross your left arm over the midline of votre corps and hold the left poignets in your right hand down at the level of your hips. Start the stretch with a bent left arm. 2. Lentement, straighten, pull, and lift it up to epaules height, as pictured. Feel this stretch originate in votre dos, not your epaules, and don''t pull too hard on the epaules joint. Switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_Wrist_Pull/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Side to Side Box Shuffle', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand to one side of the box with your left foot resting on the middle of it. 2. To begin, jump up and over to the other side of the box, landing with your right foot on top of the box and your left foot on le sol. Swing vos bras to aid your movement. 3. Continue shuffling back and forth across the box.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Side_to_Side_Box_Shuffle/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Arm Cable Crossover', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Begin by moving the pulleys to the high position, select the resistance to be used, and take a handle in each hand. 2. Step forward in front of both pulleys with vos bras extended in front of you, bringing vos mains together. Your head and poitrine should be up as you lean forward, while vos pieds should be staggered. Position de depart. 3. Keeping your left arm in place, allow your right arm to extend out to the side, maintaining a slight bend at the coudes. The right arm should be perpendicular to the body at approximately epaules level. 4. Return your arm back to the position de depart by pulling your hand back to the midline of the body. 5. Maintenez 1 seconde at the position de depart and Repetez le mouvement on the opposite side. Continue alternating back and forth for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Arm_Cable_Crossover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Arm Linear Jammer', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Position a bar into a landmine or securely anchor it in a corner. Load the bar to an appropriate poids. 2. Raise the bar from le sol, taking it to your epaules with one or both hands. Adopt a wide stance. Position de depart. 3. Perform le mouvement by extending the coudes, pressing the poids up. Move explosively, extending the hips and genoux fully to produce maximal force. 4. Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Arm_Linear_Jammer/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Arm Push-Up', 'Pectoraux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin laying prone on the ground. Move yourself into a position supporting your poids on your toes and one arm. Your working arm should be placed directly under the epaules, fully extended. vos jambes should be extended, and for this movement you may need a wider base, placing vos pieds further apart than in a normal push-up. 2. Maintain good posture, and place your free hand behind votre dos. Position de depart. 3. Lower yourself by allowing the coudes to flex until you touch the ground. 4. Descend slowly, and reverse direction be extending the arm to Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Arm_Push-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Cone Sprint Drill', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. This drill teaches quick foot action. You need a single cone. Begin standing next to the cone with one arm back and one arm forward. 2. Chop the feet as quickly as possible, blocking with the arms. Circle the cone, keep your genoux up, with violent foot action. 3. Rest after three trips around the cone.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Cone_Sprint_Drill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Leg High Box Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Position a box in a rack. Secure a band or rope in place above the box. 2. Standing in front of it, step onto the box to a full standing position, letting your other leg remain unsupported. Hold onto the band for balance 3. . Continue stepping up and down on the same leg before switching to the opposite side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Leg_High_Box_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Leg Hop Progression', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Arrange a line of cones in front of you. Assume a relaxed standing position, balanced on one leg. Raise the genoux of your opposite leg. Position de depart. 2. Hop forward, jumping and landing with the same leg over the cone. 3. Use a countermovement jump to hop from cone to cone. 4. At the end, turn around and go back on the other leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Hop_Progression/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Leg Lateral Hop', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand to the side of a cone or hurdle. To get into the start position, stand on one leg with your genoux slightly bent. 2. To begin, execute a counterjump to hop sideways over the cone. 3. Land on your jumping leg, and immediately rebound out of it by jumping back to the start position. 4. Continue hopping back and forth.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Lateral_Hop/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Leg Leg Extension', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. Seat yourself in the machine and adjust it so that you are positioned properly. The pad should be against the lower part of the shin but not in contact with the ankle. Adjust the seat so that the pivot point is in line with your genoux. Select a poids appropriate for your abilities. 2. Maintaining good posture, fully extend one leg, pausing at the top of the motion. 3. Revenez en position de depart without letting the poids stop, keeping tension on the muscle. 4. Repetez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Leg_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single-Leg Stride Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand to the side of a box with your inside foot on top of it, close to the edge. 2. Begin by swinging the arms upward as you push through the top leg, jumping upward as high as possible. Attempt to drive the opposite genoux upward. 3. Land in the same position that you started, using your inside leg to decelerate the impact.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single-Leg_Stride_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single Dumbbell Raise', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. With a wide stance, hold a dumbell with both hands, grasping the head of the halteres instead of the handle. vos bras should be extended and hanging at the waist. Position de depart. 2. Raise the poids until it is above epaules level, keeping vos bras extended. Your torse and hips should remain stationary throughout le mouvement. 3. Revenez en position de depart and Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single_Dumbbell_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single Leg Butt Kick', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin by standing on one leg, with the bent genoux raised. This will be your start position. 2. Using a countermovement jump, take off upward by extending the hip, genoux, and ankle of the grounded leg. 3. Immediately flex the genoux and attempt to touch your butt with the heel of your jumping leg. 4. Return the leg to a partially bent position underneath the hips and land. Your opposite leg should stay in relatively the same position throughout the drill.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single_Leg_Butt_Kick/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single Leg Glute Bridge', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Lay on le sol with vos pieds flat and genoux bent. 2. Raise one leg off of the ground, pulling the genoux to your poitrine. Position de depart. 3. Execute le mouvement by driving through the heel, extending your hip upward and raising your fessiers off of the ground. 4. Extend as far as possible, pause and then Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single_Leg_Glute_Bridge/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Single Leg Push-off', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand on the ground with one foot resting on the box, heel close to the edge. 2. Push off with your foot on top of the box, trying to gain as much height as possible by extending through the hip and genoux. 3. Land with the same foot on top of the box, returning your other foot back to the start position.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Single_Leg_Push-off/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sit-Up', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Allongez-vous au sol placing vos pieds either under something that will not move or by having a partner hold them. vos jambes should be bent at the genoux. 2. Place vos mains behind your head and lock them together by clasping your fingers. Position de depart. 3. Elevate your upper body so that it creates an imaginary V-shape with your cuisses. Expirez when performing this part of the exercise. 4. Once you feel the contraction for a second, lower your upper body back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sit-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sit Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds epaules width apart. Position de depart. 2. Begin le mouvement by flexing your genoux and hips, sitting back with your hips. 3. Continue until you have squatted a portion of the way down, but are above parallel, and quickly reverse the motion until you Revenez en position de depart. Repetez for 5-10 repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sit_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Skating', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Roller skating is a fun activity which can be effective in improving cardiorespiratory fitness and muscular endurance. It requires relatively good balance and coordination. It is necessary to learn the basics of skating including turning and stopping and to wear protective gear to avoid possible injury. 2. You can skate at a comfortable pace for 30 minutes straight. If you want a cardio challenge, do interval skating — speed skate two minutes of every five minutes, using the remaining three minutes to recover. A 150 lb person will typically burn about 175 calories in 30 minutes skating at a comfortable pace, similar to brisk walking.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Skating/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sled Drag - Harness', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. To begin, load the sled with the desired poids and attach the pulling strap. You can pull with handles, use a harness, or attach the pulling strap to a poids belt. 2. Whether pulling forwards or backwards, lean in the direction of travel and progress by extending through the hips and genoux.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sled_Drag_-_Harness/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sled Overhead Backward Walk', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Attach dual handles to a sled connected by a rope or chain. Load the sled to a light poids. 2. Face the sled, backing up until there is some tension in the line. Hold vos mains directly above your head with your coudes extended. Position de depart. 3. Walk backwards, keeping vos bras raised above your head. Avoid jerky movements.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sled_Overhead_Backward_Walk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sled Overhead Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Attach dual handles to a sled using a chain or rope. Load the sled to an appropriate load. 2. Facing away from the sled, step away until there is tension in the line. Raise vos mains above your head, keeping them together, palms facing each other. Your coudes should be pointed upward with the coudes flexed. Position de depart. 3. Extend through the coudes to straighten the arm. Ensure that your upper arm stays in position to isolate the triceps. 4. Upon full extension, step forward to take the slack out of the line. You may keep vos pieds staggered for more stability.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sled_Overhead_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sled Push', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Load your pushing sled with the desired poids. 2. Take an athletic posture, leaning into the sled with vos bras fully extended, grasping the handles. Push the sled as fast as possible, focusing on extending your hips and genoux to strengthen your posterior chain.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Pectoraux, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sled_Push/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sled Reverse Flye', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Attach dual handles to a sled connected by a rope or chain. Load the sled to a light poids. 2. Face the sled, backing up until there is some tension in the line. Take both handles bras tendus at about waist level. Bend the genoux slightly and keep your poitrine and head up. Position de depart. 3. Without flexing the coudes, pull the handles upward and apart, performing a reverse fly with some external rotation. Your palms should be facing forward as you do this. 4. Revenez en position de depart, taking a couple steps back to take the slack out of the line.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sled_Reverse_Flye/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sled Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Attach dual handles to a sled connected by a rope or chain. Load the sled to an appropriate poids. Face the sled, backing up until there is some tension in the line. 2. With a handle in each hand, bend the genoux slightly, keep your head and poitrine up, and begin with vos bras extended. 3. To initiate le mouvement, flex the coudes as you retract your omoplates, pulling the sled towards you. 4. Take a step or two back to get tension in the line and Repetez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sled_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sledgehammer Swings', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. You will need a tire and a sledgehammer for this exercise. Stand in front of the tire about two feet away from it with a staggered stance. Grip the sledgehammer. 2. If you are right handed, your left hand should be at the bottom of the handle, and your right hand should be choking up closer to the head. 3. As you bring the sledge up, your right hand slides toward the head; as you swing down, your right hand will slide down to join your left hand. Slam it down as hard as you can against the tire. Control the bounce of the hammer off of the tire. 4. Repetez de l autre cote.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Dos, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sledgehammer_Swings/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Incline Shoulder Raise', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Place an incline banc underneath the smith machine. Place the barre at a height that you can reach when lying down and vos bras are almost fully extended. Once the poids you need is selected, Allongez-vous sur un banc incline and make sure your epaules are aligned right under the barre. 2. Using a epaules width pronated (palms forward) grip, lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with a slight bend at the coudes. Position de depart. 3. As you Expirez, lift the bar up until vos bras are fully extended. Note: The contraction should be felt around the epaules. 4. Apres une pause, bring the bar back down to the position de depart as you Inspirez. 5. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions. 6. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Incline_Shoulder_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Behind the Back Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Machine', '1. With the bar at cuisses level, load an appropriate poids. 2. Tenez-vous debout avec the bar behind you, taking a epaules-width, pronated grip on the bar and unhook the poids. You should be standing up straight with your head and poitrine up and vos bras extended. Position de depart. 3. Initiate le mouvement by shrugging your epaules straight up. Do not flex the arms or poignets during le mouvement. 4. Apres une pause, return the poids to the position de depart. 5. Repetez for the desired number of repetitions before engaging the hooks to rack the poids.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Behind_the_Back_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Machine', '1. Place a flat banc underneath the smith machine. Now place the barre at a height that you can reach when lying down and vos bras are almost fully extended. Once the poids you need is selected, Allongez-vous sur un banc plat. Using a pronated grip that is wider than epaules width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your middle poitrine. 3. Apres une pause, bring the bar back to the position de depart as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions. 5. When you are done, lock the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Bent Over Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Machine', '1. Set the barre attached to the smith machine to a height that is about 2 inches below your genoux. 2. Bend your genoux slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to le sol. Conseil : Make sure that you keep the head up. 3. Now grasp the barre using an overhand (pronated) grip and unlock it from the smith machine rack. Then let it hang directly in front of you as vos bras hang extended perpendicular to le sol and your torse. Position de depart. 4. While keeping the torse stationary, lift the barre as you Expirez, keeping the coudes close to the body and not doing any force with the forearm other than holding the poids. On the top contracted position, squeeze the back muscles and Maintenez 1 seconde. 5. Lentement, lower the poids again to the position de depart en inspirant. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Bent_Over_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Place a block or poids plate below the bar on the Smith machine. Set the bar to a position that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step onto the plates with the balls of vos pieds and place the bar on the back of your epaules. 2. Take the bar with both hands facing forward. Rotate the bar to unrack it. Position de depart. 3. Raise your heels as high as possible by pushing off of the balls of vos pieds, flexing your calf at the top of the contraction. Your genoux should remain extended. Maintenez 1 seconde before you start to go back down. 4. Return Lentement, to the position de depart as you Inspirez while lowering your heels. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Close-Grip Bench Press', 'Triceps', 'Machine', '1. Place a flat banc underneath the smith machine. Place the barre at a height that you can reach when lying down and vos bras are almost fully extended. Once the poids you need is selected, Allongez-vous sur un banc plat. Using a close and pronated grip (palms facing forward) that is around epaules width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your middle poitrine. Conseil : Make sure that as opposed to a regular banc press, you keep the coudes close to the torse en permanence in order to maximize triceps involvement. 3. Apres une pause, bring the bar back to the position de depart as you Expirez and push the bar using your triceps muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions. 5. When you are done, lock the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Close-Grip_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Decline Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Machine', '1. Position a decline banc in the rack so that the bar will be above your poitrine. Load an appropriate poids and take your place on the banc. 2. Rotate the bar to unhook it from the rack and fully extend vos bras. votre dos should be slightly arched and your omoplates retracted. Position de depart. 3. Begin le mouvement by flexing vos bras, lowering the bar to your poitrine. 4. Pause briefly, and then extend vos bras to push the poids back to the position de depart. 5. After completing the desired number of repetitions, rotate the bar to rack the poids.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Decline_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Hang Power Clean', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Position the bar at genoux height and load it to an appropriate poids. 2. Take a pronated grip on the bar outside of epaules width and unhook the bar from the machine. vos bras should be fully extended with your head and poitrine up. Your coudes should be pointed out with your epaules back and down. Your hips should be back, loading the tension into the ischio-jambiers. Position de depart. 3. Initate le mouvement by forcefully extending the hips and genoux, accelerating into the bar. Ensure that you keep vos bras straight during this part of the motion. 4. Upon full extension, rebend the hips and genoux to lower your receiving position. 5. Allow the arms to flex at this point, rotating the coudes around the bar to receive it on your epaules. 6. Extend through the hips and genoux to come to a standing position with the bar racked on your epaules to complete le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Hang_Power_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Hip Raise', 'Abdominaux', 'Machine', '1. Position a banc in the rack and load the bar to an appropriate poids. Lie down on the banc, placing the bottom of vos pieds against the bar. Unlock the bar and extend vos jambes. You may need to use vos mains to assist you. For added stability grasp the sides of the Smith Machine. Position de depart. 2. Initiate le mouvement by rotating your pelvis, flexing your spine to raise your hips off of the banc. Maintain a slight bend in the genoux throughout the motion. 3. Apres une pause, return the hips to the banc. 4. Repetez for the desired number of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Hip_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Incline Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Machine', '1. Place an incline banc underneath the smith machine. Place the barre at a height that you can reach when lying down and vos bras are almost fully extended. Once the poids you need is selected, Allongez-vous sur un banc incline and make sure your upper poitrine is aligned with the barre. Using a pronated grip (palms facing forward) that is wider than epaules width, unlock the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your upper poitrine. 3. Apres une pause, bring the bar back to the position de depart as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions. 5. When you are done, place the bar back in the rack.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Incline_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Leg Press', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. Position a Smith machine bar a couple feet off of the ground. Ensure that it is resting on the safeties. After loading the bar to an appropriate poids, lie underneath the bar. Place the middle of vos pieds on the bar, tucking your genoux to your poitrine. Position de depart. 2. Begin le mouvement by driving through vos pieds to move the bar upward, extending the hips and genoux. Do not lock out your genoux. 3. At the top of the motion, pause briefly before returning to the position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Leg_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine One-Arm Upright Row', 'Épaules', 'Machine', '1. With the bar at cuisses level, load an appropriate poids. 2. Take a prise large on the bar and unhook the poids, removing your off hand from the bar. Your arm should be extended as you Tenez-vous debout avec your head and poitrine up. Position de depart. 3. Begin le mouvement by flexing the coudes, raising the upper arm with the coudes pointed out. Continue until your upper arm is parallel to le sol. 4. Apres une pause, return the poids to the position de depart. 5. Repetez for the desired number of repetitions before engaging the hooks to rack the poids.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_One-Arm_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Overhead Shoulder Press', 'Épaules', 'Machine', '1. To begin, place a flat banc (or preferably one with back support) underneath a smith machine. Position the barre at a height so that when seated on the flat banc, the arms must be almost fully extended to reach the barre. 2. Once you have the correct height, sit slightly in behind the barre so that there is an imaginary straight line from the tip of your nose to the barre. vos pieds should be stationary. Grab the barre with the palms facing forward, unlock it and lift it up so that vos bras are fully extended. Position de depart. 3. Lentement, begin to lower the barre until it is level with your chin while inhaling. 4. Then lift the barre back to the position de depart using your epaules while exhaling. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Overhead_Shoulder_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Pistol Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, first set the bar to a position that best matches your height. Step under it and position the bar across the back of your epaules. 2. Take the bar with vos mains facing forward, unlock it and lift it off the rack by extending vos jambes. 3 3. Move one foot forward about 12 inches in front of the bar. Extend the other leg out in front of you, holding it off the ground. Look forward en permanence and maintain a neutral or slightly arched spine. Position de depart. 4. Maintaining good posture, lower yourself by flexing the genoux and hip, going down as far as flexibility allows. 5. Pause briefly at the bottom and then Revenez en position de depart by driving through the heel of your foot, extending the genoux and hip.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Pistol_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Reverse Calf Raises', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the barre on the smith machine to fit your height and align a raised platform right under the bar. 2. Stand on the platform with the heels of vos pieds secured on top of it with the balls of vos pieds extending off it. Position your toes facing forward with a epaules width stance. 3. Now, place your epaules under the barre while maintaining the foot positioning described and push the barre up by extending your hips and genoux until your torse is standing erect. The genoux should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. Position de depart. Conseil : The barre on votre dos is only for balance purposes. 4. Raise the balls of vos pieds as you Expirez by extending your toes as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genoux is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Maintenez 1 seconde before you start to go back down. 5. Lentement, go back down to the position de depart as you Inspirez by lowering the balls of vos pieds and toes. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Reverse_Calf_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, first set the bar on the height that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck) across it. 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side (palms facing forward), unlock it and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up en permanence and also maintain a straight back. Position de depart. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section). 4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genoux as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to le sol). Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genoux should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your genoux are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genoux and the exercise has been performed incorrectly. 5. Begin to raise the bar en expirant by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Stiff-Legged Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your cuisses. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is epaules width apart. You may need some poignets wraps if using a significant amount of poids. 2. Lift the bar up by fully extending vos bras while keeping votre dos straight. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and vos jambes spaced using a epaules width or narrower stance. The genoux should be slightly bent. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the genoux stationary, lower the barre to over the top of vos pieds by bending at the waist while keeping votre dos straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from le sol until you feel a stretch on the ischio-jambiers. Exhale as you perform this movement 4. Start bringing your torse up straight again as soon as you feel the ischio-jambiers stretch by extending your hips and waist until you are back at the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this movement. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Stiff-Legged_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Machine Upright Row', 'Trapèzes', 'Machine', '1. To begin, set the bar on the smith machine to a height that is around the middle of your cuisses. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, grasp the bar using a pronated (palms forward) grip that is epaules width apart. You may need some poignets wraps if using a significant amount of poids. 2. Lift the barre up and fully extend vos bras with votre dos straight. There should be a slight bend at the coudes. Position de depart. 3. Use your side epaules to lift the bar en expirant. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the bar, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement. 4. Lower the bar back down Lentement, to the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Machine_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Smith Single-Leg Split Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, place a flat banc 2-3 feet behind the smith machine. Then, set the bar on the height that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck) across it. 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side (palms facing forward), unlock it and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Position vos jambes by placing one foot slightly forward under the bar and extending your other leg back and place the top of your foot on the banc. Position de depart. 4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genoux as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the calf becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to le sol). Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genoux should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your genoux is past that imaginary line (if it is past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genoux and the exercise has been performed incorrectly. 5. Begin to raise the bar en expirant by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten your leg again and go back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 7. Switch legs and Repetez le mouvement.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Smith_Single-Leg_Split_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Place vos pieds at a epaules width stance with the barre resting right above the connection between the toes and the rest of the foot. 2. With a palms facing down grip, bend at the genoux and keeping the back flat grab the bar using a wider than epaules width grip. Bring the hips down and make sure that votre corps drops as if you were going to sit on a chair. Position de depart. 3. Start pushing le sol as if it were a moving platform with vos pieds and simultaneously start lifting the barre keeping it close to vos jambes. 4. As the bar reaches the middle of your cuisses, push le sol with vos jambes and lift votre corps to a complete extension in an explosive motion. 5. Lift your epaules back in a shrugging movement as you bring the bar up while lifting your coudes out to the side and keeping them above the bar for as long as possible. 6. Now in a very quick but powerful motion, you have to get votre corps under the barre when it has reached a high enough point where it can be controlled and drop while locking vos bras and holding the barre overhead as you assume a squat position. 7. Finalize le mouvement by rising up out of the squat position to finish the lift. At the end of the lift both feet should be on line and the arms fully extended holding the barre overhead.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Balance', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with the feet in the pulling position, the bar racked across the back of the epaules, and the hands placed in a wide snatch grip. 2. Pop the bar with an abrupt dip and drive of the genoux, and aggressively drive under the bar, transitioning the feet into the receiving position. 3. Receive the bar locked out overhead near the bottom of the squat. The torse should remain vertical, lowering the hips between the legs. 4. Continue to descend to full depth, and return to a standing position. Carefully lower the poids.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Balance/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. The snatch deadlift strengthens the first pull of the snatch. Begin with a wide snatch grip with the barre placed on the platform. The feet should be directly under the hips, with the feet turned out. Squat down to the bar, keeping the back in absolute extension with the head facing forward. 2. Initiate le mouvement by driving through the heels, raising the hips. The back angle should remain the same until the bar passes the genoux. 3. At that point, drive your hips through the bar as you lay back. Return the bar to the platform by reversing the motion.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Pull', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take a wide snatch grip. Lower your hips with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your epaules just in front of the bar. Position de depart. 2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genoux. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genoux. 3. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the pull. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisses position, begin extending through the hips. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hips, genoux, and ankles, using speed to move the bar upward. 4. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back. Full extension should be violent and abrupt, and ensure that you do not prolong the extension for longer than necessary.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Pull/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch Shrug', 'Trapèzes', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a prise large, with the bar hanging at the mid cuisses position. You can use a hook or prise en pronation. votre dos should be straight and inclined slightly forward. 2. Shrug your epaules towards your ears. While this exercise can usually by loaded with heavier poids than a snatch, avoid overloading to the point that the execution slows down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_Shrug/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Snatch from Blocks', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a loaded barre on boxes or stands of the desired height. A prise large should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the poitrine up and the head looking forward. The epaules should be just in front of the bar, with the coudes pointed out. This will be the position de depart. 2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the boxes. 3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips genoux and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the epaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side. 4. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move to just outside the hips, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar with votre corps as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead. 5. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and poitrine up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the poids to the boxes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Snatch_from_Blocks/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Speed Band Overhead Triceps', 'Triceps', 'Élastique', '1. For this exercise anchor a band to the ground. We used an incline banc and anchored the band to the base, standing over the banc. Alternatively, this could be performed standing on the band. 2. To begin, pull the band behind your head, holding it with a pronated grip and your coudes up. Position de depart. 3. To perform le mouvement, extend through the coudes to to straighten vos bras, ensuring that you keep your upper arm in place. 4. Pause, and then Revenez en position de depart.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Speed_Band_Overhead_Triceps/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Speed Box Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Attach bands to the bar that are securely anchored near the ground. You may need to choke the bands to get adequate tension. 2. Use a box of an appropriate height for this exercise. Load the bar to a poids that still requires effort, but isn''t so heavy that speed is compromised. Typically, that will be between 50-70% of your one rep max. 3. Position the bar on your upper back, omoplates retracted, back arched and everything tight head to toe. This will be the position de depart. 4. Unrack the bar and position yourself in front of the box. Sit back with your hips until you are seated on the box, ensuring that you descend under control and don''t crash onto the surface. 5. Pause briefly, and explode off of the box, extending through the hips and genoux.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Speed_Box_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Speed Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck) across it. 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. Position de depart. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section). 4. Begin to lower the bar by bending the genoux as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to le sol). Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genoux should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your genoux are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genoux and the exercise has been performed incorrectly. 5. Begin to raise the bar as fast as possible without involving momentum en expirant by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de depart. Note: You should perform these exercises as fast as possible but without breaking perfect form and without involving momentum. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Speed_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spell Caster', 'Abdominaux', 'Haltères', '1. Hold a halteres in each hand with a pronated grip. vos pieds should be wide with your hips and genoux extended. Position de depart. 2. Begin le mouvement by pulling both of the halteres to one side next to your hip, rotating your torse. 3. Keeping vos bras straight and the halteres parallel to the ground, rotate your torse to swing the poids to your opposite side. 4. Continue alternating, rotating from one side to the other until the set is complete.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spell_Caster/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spider Crawl', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a prone position on le sol. Support your poids on vos mains and toes, with vos pieds together and votre corps straight. vos bras should be bent to 90 degrees. Position de depart. 2. Initiate le mouvement by raising one foot off of the ground. Externally rotate the leg and bring the genoux toward your coudes, as far forward as possible. 3. Return this leg to the position de depart and Repetez de l autre cote.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spider_Crawl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spider Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre EZ', '1. Start out by setting the bar on the part of the preacher banc that you would normally sit on. Make sure to align the barre properly so that it is balanced and will not fall off. 2. Move to the front side of the preacher banc (the part where the arms usually lay) and position yourself to lay at a 45 degree slant with your torse and stomach pressed against the front side of the preacher banc. 3. Make sure that vos pieds (especially the toes) are well positioned on le sol and place your upper arms on top of the pad located on the inside part of the preacher banc. 4. Use vos bras to grab the barre with a supinated grip (palms facing up) at about epaules width apart or slightly closer from each other. 5. Lentement, begin to lift the barre upwards and exhale. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. 6. Lentement, begin to bring the barre back to the position de depart as your Inspirez. . 7. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spider_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Spinal Stretch', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Sit in a chair so votre dos is straight and vos pieds planted on le sol. 2. Interlace your fingers behind your head, coudes out and your chin down. 3. Twist your upper body to one side about 3 times as far as you can. Then lean forward and twist your torse to reach your coudes to le sol on the inside of your genoux. 4. Return to upright position and then Repetez for your other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Bas du dos, Cou, Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Spinal_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Clean', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. With a barre on le sol close to the shins, take an prise en pronation just outside the legs. Lower your hips with the poids focused on the heels, back straight, head facing forward, poitrine up, with your epaules just in front of the bar. Position de depart. 2. Begin the first pull by driving through the heels, extending your genoux. votre dos angle should stay the same, and vos bras should remain straight. Move the poids with control as you continue to above the genoux. 3. Next comes the second pull, the main source of acceleration for the clean. As the bar approaches the mid-cuisses position, begin extending through the hips. In a jumping motion, accelerate by extending the hips, genoux, and ankles, using speed to move the bar upward. There should be no need to actively pull through the arms to accelerate the poids; at the end of the second pull, the body should be fully extended, leaning slightly back, with the arms still extended. 4. As full extension is achieved, transition into the third pull by aggressively shrugging and flexing the arms with the coudes up and out. At peak extension, aggressively pull yourself down, rotating your coudes under the bar as you do so. 5. Receive the bar with the feet split, aggressively moving one foot forward and one foot back. The bar should be racked onto the protracted epaules, lightly touching the throat with the hands relaxed. Continue to descend to the bottom position, which will help in the recovery. 6. Immediately recover by driving through the heels, keeping the torse upright and coudes up. Bring the feet together as you stand up.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Jerk', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing with the poids racked on the front of the epaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hips, flex the genoux without moving the hips backward. 2. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move your head out of the way as the bar leaves the epaules. At this moment as the feet leave le sol, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. 3. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athlete''s effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should be moved to a split stance, one foot forward, one foot back, with the genoux partially bent. Receive the bar with the arms locked out overhead. 4. Return to a standing position, bringing the feet together.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Assume a lunge stance position with one foot forward with the genoux bent, and the rear genoux nearly touching the ground. 2. Ensure that the front genoux is over the midline of the foot. 3. Extending through both legs, jump as high as possible, swinging vos bras to gain lift. 4. As you jump, bring vos pieds together, and move them back to their initial positions as you land. 5. Absorb the impact by reverting back to the position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Snatch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a loaded barre on le sol. The bar should be close to or touching the shins, and a prise large should be taken on the bar. The feet should be directly below the hips, with the feet turned out as needed. Lower the hips, with the poitrine up and the head looking forward. The epaules should be just in front of the bar. This will be the position de depart. 2. Begin the first pull by driving through the front of the heels, raising the bar from the ground. The back angle should stay the same until the bar passes the genoux. 3. Transition into the second pull by extending through the hips genoux and ankles, driving the bar up as quickly as possible. The bar should be close to the body. At peak extension, shrug the epaules and allow the coudes to flex to the side. 4. As you move vos pieds into the receiving position, forcefully pull yourself below the bar as you elevate the bar overhead. The feet should move forcefully to a split position, one foot forward one foot back. Receive the bar with votre corps as low as possible and the arms fully extended overhead. 5. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and poitrine up, drive through heels of the feet to move to a standing position, bringing vos pieds together. 6. Carefully return the poids to floor.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Quadriceps, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Snatch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Squat with Dumbbells', 'Quadriceps', 'Haltères', '1. Position yourself into a staggered stance with the rear foot elevated and front foot forward. 2. Hold a halteres in each hand, letting them hang at the sides. Position de depart. 3. Begin by descending, flexing your genoux and hip to lower votre corps down. Maintain good posture througout le mouvement. Keep the front genoux in line with the foot as you perform the exercise. 4. At the bottom of le mouvement, drive through the heel to extend the genoux and hip to Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Squat_with_Dumbbells/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Split Squats', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Being in a standing position. Jump into a split leg position, with one leg forward and one leg back, flexing the genoux and lowering your hips slightly as you do so. 2. As you descend, immediately reverse direction, standing back up and jumping, reversing the position of vos jambes. Repetez 5-10 times on each leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Split_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat Jerk', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing with the poids racked on the front of the epaules, begin with the dip. With vos pieds directly under your hips, flex the genoux without moving the hips backward. Go down only slightly, and reverse direction as powerfully as possible. Drive through the heels create as much speed and force as possible, and be sure to move your head out of the way as the bar leaves the epaules. 2. At this moment as the feet leave le sol, the feet must be placed into the receiving position as quickly as possible. In the brief moment the feet are not actively driving against the platform, the athlete''s effort to push the bar up will drive them down. The feet should move forcefully to just outside the hips, turned out as necessary. Receive the bar with votre corps in a full squat and the arms fully extended overhead. 3. Keeping the bar aligned over the front of the heels, your head and poitrine up, drive throught heels of the feet to move to a standing position. Carefully return the poids to floor.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat with Bands', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Set up the bands on the sleeves, secured to either band pegs, the rack, or halteres so that there is appropriate tension. 2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the epaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your epaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wide for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers. Keep your head facing forward. 3. With votre dos, epaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genoux and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torse lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hip being in line with the top of the genoux. 4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genoux out, drive upward as you lead le mouvement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat with Chains', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. To set up the chains, begin by looping the leader chain over the sleeves of the bar. The heavy chain should be attached using a snap hook. Adjust the length of the lead chain so that a few links are still on le sol at the top of le mouvement. 2. Begin by stepping under the bar and placing it across the back of the epaules. Squeeze your omoplates together and rotate your coudes forward, attempting to bend the bar across your epaules. Remove the bar from the rack, creating a tight arch in your lower back, and step back into position. Place vos pieds wide for more emphasis on the back, fessiers, adductors, and ischio-jambiers. Keep your head facing forward. 3. With votre dos, epaules, and sangle abdominale tight, push your genoux and butt out and you begin your descent. Sit back with your hips as much as possible. Ideally, your shins should be perpendicular to the ground. Lower bar position necessitates a greater torse lean to keep the bar over the heels. Continue until you break parallel, which is defined as the crease of the hip being in line with the top of the genoux. 4. Keeping the poids on your heels and pushing vos pieds and genoux out, drive upward as you lead le mouvement with your head. Continue upward, maintaining tightness head to toe, until you have returned to the position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squat with Plate Movers', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. To begin, first set the bar on a rack to just below epaules level. Position a poids plate on the ground a couple feet back from the rack. Once the bar is loaded, step under it and place the back of your epaules across it. 2. Hold on to the bar with both hands and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straighten your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and adopt a wide stance with the toes slightly pointed out, with one foot on the poids plate. Keep your head up en permanence. Position de depart. 4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genoux and hips. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees. 5. Raise the bar en expirant by pushing le sol with the heels of vos pieds as you extend the hips and genoux. 6. At the top of le mouvement, side step, bringing vos pieds together on the opposite side of the plate. 7. Using your inside foot, push the poids plate, sliding it across le sol to where you were just standing. 8. Place your inside foot on the poids plate, adopting a wide stance for the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squat_with_Plate_Movers/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Squats - With Bands', 'Quadriceps', 'Élastique', '1. To start out, make sure that the exercise band is at an even split between both the left and right side of the body. To do this, use vos mains to grab both sides of the band and place both feet in the middle of the band. vos pieds should be epaules width apart from each other. 2. When holding the bands, they should be the same height on each side. You should be using a pronated grip (palms facing forward) and have the handles of the bands next to your face for this exercise. Position de depart. 3. Lentement, start to bend the genoux and lower the legs so that your cuisses are parallel to le sol while exhaling. 4. Use the heel of vos pieds to push votre corps up to the position de depart en expirant. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Squats_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stairmaster', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the stairmaster and select the desired option from the menu. You can choose a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. 2. Pump vos jambes up and down in an established rhythm, driving the pedals down but not all the way to le sol. It is recommended that you maintain your grip on the handles so that you don''t fall. The handles can be used to monitor your heart rate to help you stay at an appropriate intensity. 3. Stairmasters offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than running outside. They are typically much harder than other cardio equipment. A 150 lb person will typically burn over 300 calories in 30 minutes, compared to about 175 calories walking.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stairmaster/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Alternating Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a halteres in each hand. Raise the halteres to your epaules with your palms facing forward and your coudes pointed out. Position de depart. 2. Extend one arm to press the halteres straight up, keeping your off hand in place. Do not lean or jerk the poids during le mouvement. 3. Apres une pause, return the poids to the position de depart. 4. Repetez de l autre cote, continuing to alternate between arms.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Alternating_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Barbell Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the bar on the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck). 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. The genoux should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. Position de depart. Conseil : For better range of motion you may also place the ball of vos pieds on a wooden block but be careful as this option requires more balance and a sturdy block. 4. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your ankles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genoux is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down. 5. Go back Lentement, to the position de depart as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the ankles until mollets are stretched. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Barbell_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Barbell Press Behind Neck', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for easier pick up of the bar. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck) across it. 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. votre dos should be kept straight while performing this exercise. Position de depart. 4. Elevate the barre overhead by fully extending vos bras while breathing out. 5. Hold the contraction for a second and lower the barre back down to the position de depart by inhaling. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Barbell_Press_Behind_Neck/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Bent-Over One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. With a halteres in one hand and the palm facing your torse, bend your genoux slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to le sol. Make sure that you keep the head up. 2. The upper arm should be close to the torse and parallel to le sol while the forearm is pointing towards le sol as the hand holds the poids. Conseil : There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearm and the upper arm. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids en expirant until the forearms are parallel to le sol and the whole arm is extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves. 4. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the halteres back to the position de depart en inspirant. 5. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions. 6. Switch arms and Repetez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Bent-Over_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Bent-Over Two-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. With a halteres in each hand and the palms facing your torse, bend your genoux slightly and bring your torse forward, by bending at the waist, while keeping the back straight until it is almost parallel to le sol. Make sure that you keep the head up. The upper arms should be close to the torse and parallel to le sol while the forearms are pointing towards le sol as the hands hold the poids. Conseil : There should be a 90-degree angle between the forearms and the upper arm. Position de depart. 2. Keeping the upper arms stationary, use the triceps to lift the poids en expirant until the forearms are parallel to le sol and the whole arms are extended. Like many other arm exercises, only the forearm moves. 3. After a second contraction at the top, Lentement, lower the halteres back to their position de depart en inspirant. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Bent-Over_Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Biceps Cable Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding a cable curl bar that is attached to a low pulley. Grab the cable bar at epaules width and keep the coudes close to the torse. The palm of vos mains should be facing up (supinated grip). Position de depart. 2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the bar is at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the muscle. 3. Lentement, begin to bring the curl bar back to position de depart as your Inspirez. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Biceps_Cable_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Biceps Stretch', 'Biceps', 'Autre', '1. Clasp vos mains behind votre dos with your palms together, straighten arms and then rotate them so your palms face downward. 2. Raise vos bras up and hold until you feel a stretch in your biceps.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Biceps_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Bradford Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Place a loaded bar at epaules level in a rack. With a pronated grip at epaules width, begin with the bar racked across the front of your epaules. Position de depart. 2. Initiate the lift by extending the coudes to press the bar overhead. Avoid locking out the coudes as you move the poids behind your head. 3. Lower the bar down to the back of the head until your coudes forms a right angle. 4. Lift the bar back over your head by extending the coudes 5. Lower the bar down to the position de depart. 6. Alternate in this manner until you complete the recommended amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Bradford_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Cable Chest Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Poulie', '1. Position dual pulleys to poitrine height and select an appropriate poids. Stand a foot or two in front of the cables, holding one in each hand. You can stagger your stance for better stability. 2. Position the upper arm at a 90 degree angle with the omoplates together. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the rest of the body stationary, extend through the coudes to press the handles forward, drawing them together in front of you. 4. Pause at the top of the motion, and Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Chest_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Cable Lift', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle on a tower, and move the cable to the lowest pulley position. 2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with one hand and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable. Your outstretched arm should be aligned with the cable. 3. With vos pieds positioned epaules width apart, squat down and grab the handle with both hands. vos bras should still be fully extended. 4. In one motion, pull the handle up and across votre corps until vos bras are in a fully-extended position above your head. 5. Keep votre dos straight and vos bras close to votre corps as you pivot votre dos foot and straighten vos jambes to get a full range of motion. 6. Retract vos bras and then votre corps. Return to the neutral position in a slow and controlled manner. 7. Repetez to failure. 8. Then, reposition and Repetez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Lift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Cable Wood Chop', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Connect a standard handle to a tower, and move the cable to the highest pulley position. 2. With your side to the cable, grab the handle with one hand and step away from the tower. You should be approximately arm''s length away from the pulley, with the tension of the poids on the cable. Your outstretched arm should be aligned with the cable. 3. With vos pieds positioned epaules width apart, reach upward with your other hand and grab the handle with both hands. vos bras should still be fully extended. 4. In one motion, pull the handle down and across votre corps to your front genoux while rotating your torse. 5. Keep votre dos and arms straight and sangle abdominale tight while you pivot votre dos foot and bend your genoux to get a full range of motion. 6. Maintain your stance and straight arms. Return to the neutral position in a slow and controlled manner. 7. Repetez to failure. 8. Then, reposition and Repetez the same series of movements on the opposite side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Cable_Wood_Chop/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Calf Raises', 'Mollets', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the padded lever of the calf raise machine to fit your height. 2. Place your epaules under the pads provided and position your toes facing forward (or using any of the two other positions described at the beginning of the chapter). The balls of vos pieds should be secured on top of the calf block with the heels extending off it. Push the lever up by extending your hips and genoux until your torse is standing erect. The genoux should be kept with a slight bend; never locked. Toes should be facing forward, outwards or inwards as described at the beginning of the chapter. Position de depart. 3. Raise your heels as you Expirez by extending your ankles as high as possible and flexing your calf. Ensure that the genoux is kept stationary en permanence. There should be no bending at any time. Hold the contracted position by a second before you start to go back down. 4. Go back Lentement, to the position de depart as you Inspirez by lowering your heels as you bend the ankles until mollets are stretched. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Calf_Raises/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Concentration Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Taking a halteres in your working hand, lean forward. Allow your working arm to hang perpendicular to the ground with the coudes pointing out. Position de depart. 2. Flex the coudes to curl the poids, keeping the upper arm stationary. At the top of the repetition, flex the biceps and pause. 3. Lower the halteres back to the position de depart. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Concentration_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Calf Raise', 'Mollets', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright holding two halteres in vos mains by your sides. Place the ball of the foot on a sturdy and stable wooden board (that is around 2-3 inches tall) while your heels extend off and touch le sol. Position de depart. 2. With the toes pointing either straight (to hit all parts equally), inwards (for emphasis on the outer head) or outwards (for emphasis on the inner head), raise the heels off le sol en expirant by contracting the mollets. Hold the top contraction for a second. 3. en inspirant, go back to the position de depart by Lentement, lowering the heels. 4. Repetez for the recommended amount of times.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Calf_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Standing with vos pieds epaules width apart, take a halteres in each hand. Raise the halteres to head height, the coudes out and about 90 degrees. Position de depart. 2. Maintaining strict technique with no leg drive or leaning back, extend through the coudes to raise the poids together directly above your head. 3. Pause, and Lentement, return the poids to the position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Reverse Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a halteres in each hand using a pronated grip (palms facing down). vos bras should be fully extended while vos pieds are epaules width apart from each other. Position de depart. 2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the muscle. 3. Lentement, begin to bring the halteres back to position de depart as your Inspirez. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Reverse_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Straight-Arm Front Delt Raise Above Head', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Hold the halteres in front of your cuisses, palms facing your cuisses. 2. Keep vos bras straight with a slight bend at the coudes but keep them locked. Position de depart. 3. Raise the halteres in a semicircular motion to arm''s length overhead en expirant. 4. Lentement, Revenez en position de depart using the same path en inspirant. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Straight-Arm_Front_Delt_Raise_Above_Head/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a halteres held by both hands. vos pieds should be about epaules width apart from each other. Lentement, use both hands to grab the halteres and lift it over your head until both arms are fully extended. 2. The resistance should be resting in the palms of vos mains with your thumbs around it. The palm of the hands should be facing up towards the ceiling. Position de depart. 3. Keeping your upper arms close to your head with coudes in and perpendicular to le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step. 4. Go back to the position de depart by using the triceps to raise the halteres. Expirez as you perform this step. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Dumbbell Upright Row', 'Trapèzes', 'Haltères', '1. Grasp a halteres in each hand with a pronated (palms forward) grip that is slightly less than epaules width. The halteres should be resting on top of your cuisses. vos bras should be extended with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos should be straight. Position de depart. 2. Use your side epaules to lift the halteres en expirant. The halteres should be close to the body as you move it up and the coudes should drive the motion. Continue to lift them until they nearly touch your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the halteres, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement. 3. Lower the halteres back down Lentement, to the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Dumbbell_Upright_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Elevated Quad Stretch', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Start by standing with votre dos about two to three feet away from a banc or step. 2. Lift one leg behind you and rest your foot on the step,either on your instep or the ball of your foot, whichever you find most comfortable. 3. Keep your supporting genoux slightly bent and avoid letting that genoux extend out beyond your toes. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Elevated_Quad_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Front Barbell Raise Over Head', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a barre in vos mains. You should grip the bar with palms facing down and a closer than epaules width grip apart from each other. 2. vos pieds should be epaules width apart from each other. Your coudes should be slightly bent. Position de depart. 3. Lift the barre up until it is directly over your head while exhaling. Make sure to keep your coudes slightly bent when performing each repetition. 4. Once you feel the contraction, begin to lower the barre back down to the position de depart en inspirant. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Front_Barbell_Raise_Over_Head/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Gastrocnemius Calf Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Place your right heel on a step with your genoux extended and lean forward to grab your right toe with your right hand. Your left genoux should be slightly bent and votre dos should be straight. 2. Support your poids on your left leg and place your left hand on your left cuisses. 3. Pull your right toes toward your genoux until you feel a stretch in your calf.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Gastrocnemius_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Hamstring and Calf Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Being by looping a belt, band, or rope around one foot. While standing, place that foot forward. 2. Bend votre dos leg, while keeping the front one straight. Now raise the toes of your front foot off of the ground and lean forward. 3. Using the belt, pull on the top of the foot to increase the stretch in the calf. Hold for 10-20 seconds and Repetez with the other foot.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Hamstring_and_Calf_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Hip Circles', 'Abducteurs', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin standing on one leg, holding to a vertical support. 2. Raise the unsupported genoux to 90 degrees. Position de depart. 3. Open the hip as far as possible, attempting to make a big circle with your genoux. 4. Perform this movement Lentement, for a number of repetitions, and Repetez de l autre cote.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Hip_Circles/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Hip Flexors', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec the spine vertical, the left foot slightly in front of the right. 2. Bend both genoux and lift the back heel off le sol as you press the right hip forward. You can''t get a thorough, deep stretch in this position, however, because it''s hard to relax the hip flexor and stand on it at the same time. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Hip_Flexors/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Inner-Biceps Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec a halteres in each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse. vos jambes should be at about epaules''s width apart from each other. 2. Rotate the palms of the hands so that they are facing inward in a neutral position. Position de depart. 3. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids out while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Your poignets should turn so that when the poids are fully elevated you have supinated grip (palms facing up). 4. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules level. Conseil : Keep the forearms aligned with your outer deltoids. 5. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. 6. Lentement, begin to bring the halteres back to the position de depart as your Inspirez. Remember to rotate the poignets as you lower the poids in order to switch back to a neutral grip. 7. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Inner-Biceps_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Lateral Stretch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Take a slightly wider than hip distance stance with your genoux slightly bent. 2. Place your right hand on your right hip to support the spine. 3. Raise your left arm in a vertical line and place your left hand behind your head. Keep it there as you incline your torse to the right. 4. Keep your poids evenly distributed between both legs (don''t lean into your left hip). Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Lateral_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Leg Curl', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Machine', '1. Adjust the machine lever to fit your height and lie with your torse bent at the waist facing forward around 30-45 degrees (since an angled position is more favorable for ischio-jambiers recruitment) with the pad of the lever on the back of your right leg (just a few inches under the mollets) and the front of the right leg on top of the machine pad. 2. Keeping the torse bent forward, ensure your leg is fully stretched and grab the side handles of the machine. Position your toes straight. Position de depart. 3. en expirant, curl your right leg up as far as possible without lifting the upper leg from the pad. Once you hit the entierement contracte position, hold it for a second. 4. en inspirant, bring the legs back to the initial position. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 5. Perform the same exercise now for the left leg.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Leg_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Long Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. This drill is best done in sand or other soft landing surface. Ensure that you are able to measure distance. Stand in a partial squat stance with feet epaules width apart. 2. Utilizing a big arm swing and a countermovement of the legs, jump forward as far as you can. 3. Attempt to land with vos pieds out in front you, reaching as far as possible with vos jambes. 4. Measure the distance from your landing point to the starting point and track results.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Long_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Low-Pulley Deltoid Raise', 'Épaules', 'Poulie', '1. Start by standing to the right side of a low pulley row. Use your left hand to come across the body and grab a single handle attached to the low pulley with a pronated grip (palms facing down). Rest your arm in front of you. Your right hand should grab the machine for better support and balance. 2. Make sure that votre dos is erect and vos pieds are epaules width apart from each other. Position de depart. 3. Begin to use the left hand and come across votre corps out until it is elevated to epaules height while exhaling. 4. Feel the contraction at the top for a second and begin to Lentement, lower the handle back down to the original position de depart while inhaling. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 6. Switch arms and Repetez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Low-Pulley_Deltoid_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Low-Pulley One-Arm Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Grab a single handle with your left arm next to the low pulley machine. Turn away from the machine keeping the handle to the side of votre corps with your arm fully extended. Now use both hands to elevate the single handle directly above the head with the palm facing forward. Keep your upper arm completely vertical (perpendicular to le sol) and put your right hand on your left coudes to help keep it steady. Position de depart. 2. Keeping your upper arms close to your head (coudes in) and perpendicular to le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step. 3. Go back to the position de depart by using the triceps to raise the single handle. Expirez as you perform this step. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 5. Switch arms and Repetez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Low-Pulley_One-Arm_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Military Press', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Start by placing a barre that is about poitrine high on a squat rack. Once you have selected the poids, grab the barre using a pronated (palms facing forward) grip. Make sure to grip the bar wider than epaules width apart from each other. 2. Slightly bend the genoux and place the barre on your collar bone. Lift the barre up keeping it lying on your poitrine. Take a step back and position vos pieds epaules width apart from each other. 3. Once you pick up the barre with the correct grip length, lift the bar up over your head by locking vos bras. Hold at about epaules level and slightly in front of your head. Position de depart. 4. Lower the bar down to the collarbone Lentement, en inspirant. 5. Lift the bar back up to the position de depart en expirant. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Military_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Olympic Plate Hand Squeeze', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. To begin, stand straight while holding a poids plate by the ridge at arm''s length in each hand using a neutral grip (palms facing in). You feet should be epaules width apart from each other. Position de depart. 2. Lower the plates until the fingers are nearly extended but can still hold poids. Inhale as you lower the plates. 3. Now raise the plates back to the position de depart en expirant by closing vos mains. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. prescribed in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Olympic_Plate_Hand_Squeeze/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing One-Arm Cable Curl', 'Biceps', 'Poulie', '1. Start out by grabbing single handle next to the low pulley machine. Make sure you are far enough from the machine so that your arm is supporting the poids. 2. Make sure that your upper arm is stationary, perpendicular to le sol with coudes in and palms facing forward. Your non lifting arm should be grabbing your waist. This will allow you to keep your balance. 3. Lentement, begin to curl the single handle upwards while keeping the upper arm stationary until your forearm touches your biceps while exhaling. Conseil : Only the forearm should move. 4. Hold the contraction position as you squeeze the biceps and then lower the single handle back down to the position de depart en inspirant. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 6. Switch arms while performing this exercise.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Cable_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing One-Arm Dumbbell Curl Over Incline Bench', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Stand on the back side of an incline banc as if you were going to be a spotter for someone. Have a halteres in one hand and rest it across the incline banc with a supinated (palms up) grip. 2. Position your non lifting hand at the corner or side of the incline banc. The poitrine should be pressed against the top part of the incline and vos pieds should be pressed against le sol at a wide stance. Position de depart. 3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the halteres upward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres is at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde. 4. Lentement, begin to bring the halteres back to position de depart as your Inspirez. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 6. Switch arms while performing this exercise.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Curl_Over_Incline_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing One-Arm Dumbbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec a halteres held in one hand. vos pieds should be about epaules width apart from each other. Now fully extend the arm with the halteres over your head. Conseil : The small finger of your hand should be facing the ceiling and the palm of your hand should be facing forward. The halteres should be above your head. 2. Position de depart. 3. Keeping your upper arm close to your head (coudes in) and perpendicular to le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearm touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arm should remain stationary and only the forearm should move. Inspirez as you perform this step. 4. Go back to the position de depart by using the triceps to raise the halteres. Expirez as you perform this step. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 6. Switch arms and Repetez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Overhead Barbell Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Barre', '1. To begin, stand up holding a barre or e-z bar using a pronated grip (palms facing forward) with vos mains closer than epaules width apart from each other. vos pieds should be about epaules width apart. 2. Now elevate the barre above your head until vos bras are fully extended. Keep your coudes in. Position de depart. 3. Keeping your upper arms close to your head and coudes in, perpendicular to le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step. 4. Go back to the position de depart by using the triceps to raise the barre. Expirez as you perform this step. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Overhead_Barbell_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Palm-In One-Arm Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Start by having a halteres in one hand with your arm fully extended to the side using a neutral grip. Use your other arm to hold on to an incline banc to keep your balance. 2. vos pieds should be epaules width apart from each other. Now Lentement, lift the halteres up until you create a 90 degree angle with your arm. Note: Your forearm should be perpendicular to le sol. Continue to maintain a neutral grip throughout the entire exercise. 3. Lentement, lift the halteres up until your arm is fully extended. This the position de depart. 4. While inhaling lower the poids down until your arm is at a 90 degree angle again. 5. Feel the contraction for a second and then lift the poids back up towards the position de depart while exhaling. Remember to hold on to the incline banc and keep vos pieds positioned to keep balance during the exercise. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 7. Switch arms and Repetez the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Palm-In_One-Arm_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Palms-In Dumbbell Press', 'Épaules', 'Haltères', '1. Start by having a halteres in each hand with your arm fully extended to the side using a neutral grip. vos pieds should be epaules width apart from each other. Now Lentement, lift the halteres up until you create a 90 degree angle with vos bras. Note: Your forearms should be perpendicular to le sol. This the position de depart. 2. Continue to maintain a neutral grip throughout the entire exercise. Lentement, lift the halteres up until vos bras are fully extended. 3. While inhaling lower the poids down until your arm is at a 90 degree angle again. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Palms-In_Dumbbell_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Palms-Up Barbell Behind The Back Wrist Curl', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Start by standing straight and holding a barre behind your fessiers at arm''s length while using a pronated grip (palms will be facing back away from the fessiers) and having vos mains epaules width apart from each other. 2. You should be looking straight forward while vos pieds are epaules width apart from each other. Position de depart. 3. While exhaling, Lentement, elevate the barre up by curling your poignets in a semi-circular motion towards the ceiling. Note: Your poignets should be the only body part moving for this exercise. 4. Hold the contraction for a second and lower the barre back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 6. When finished, lower the barre down to the squat rack or le sol by bending the genoux. Conseil : It is easiest to either pick it up from a squat rack or have a partner hand it to you.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Palms-Up_Barbell_Behind_The_Back_Wrist_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Pelvic Tilt', 'Bas du dos', 'Autre', '1. Start off with vos pieds hip-distance apart. 2. Bend your genoux slightly to keep them soft and springy. 3. You may want to move your pelvis forward and backward and back few times before holding the tailbone forward in this stretch.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Pelvic_Tilt/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Rope Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to a high pulley and select an appropriate poids. 2. Tenez-vous debout avec votre dos to the cable tower. Take the rope with both hands over your epaules, holding it to your upper poitrine. Position de depart. 3. Perform le mouvement by flexing the spine, crunching the poids down as far as you can. 4. Hold the peak contraction for a moment before returning to the position de depart.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Rope_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Soleus And Achilles Stretch', 'Mollets', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds hip-distance apart, one foot slightly in front of the other. 2. Bend both genoux, keeping votre dos heel on le sol. Switch sides.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Soleus_And_Achilles_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Toe Touches', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec some space in front and behind you. 2. Bend at the waist, keeping vos jambes straight, until you can relax and let your upper body hang down in front of you. Let vos bras and hands hang down naturally. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Toe_Touches/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Towel Triceps Extension', 'Triceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec both arms fully extended above the head holding one end of a towel with both hands. Your coudes should be in and the arms perpendicular to le sol with the palms facing each other while vos pieds should be epaules width apart from each other. Position de depart. 2. Now communicate with your partner so that he/she can grip the other side of the towel to apply resistance. Keeping your upper arms close to your head (coudes in) and perpendicular to le sol, lower the resistance in a semicircular motion behind your head until your forearms touch your biceps. Conseil : The upper arms should remain stationary and only the forearms should move. Inspirez as you perform this step. 3. Go back to the position de depart by using the triceps to raise the towel. Expirez as you perform this step. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Towel_Triceps_Extension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Standing Two-Arm Overhead Throw', 'Épaules', 'Medecine ball', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds epaules width apart holding a medicine ball in both hands. To begin, reach the medicine ball deep behind your head as you bend the genoux slightly and lean back. 2. Violently throw the ball forward, flexing at the hip and using your whole body to complete le mouvement. 3. The medicine ball can be thrown to a partner or to a wall, receiving it as it bounces back.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Standing_Two-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Star Jump', 'Quadriceps', 'Poids de corps', '1. Begin in a relaxed stance with vos pieds epaules width apart and hold vos bras close to the body. 2. To initiate the move, squat down halfway and explode back up as high as possible. Fully extend your entire body, spreading vos jambes and arms away from the body. 3. As you land, bring your limbs back in and absorb your impact through the legs.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Star_Jump/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Step-up with Knee Raise', 'Fessiers', 'Poids de corps', '1. Stand facing a box or banc of an appropriate height with vos pieds together. Position de depart. 2. Begin le mouvement by stepping up, putting your left foot on the top of the banc. Extend through the hip and genoux of your front leg to stand up on the box. As you stand on the box with your left leg, flex your right genoux and hip, bringing your genoux as high as you can. 3. Reverse this motion to step down off the box, and then Repetez the sequence on the opposite leg.', 'Muscles secondaires : Ischio-jambiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Step-up_with_Knee_Raise/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Step Mill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the stepmill and select the desired option from the menu. You can choose a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Use caution so that you don''t trip as you climb the stairs. It is recommended that you maintain your grip on the handles so that you don''t fall. 2. Stepmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than running outside while offering a similar rate of calories burned. They are typically much harder than other cardio equipment. A 150 lb person will typically burn over 300 calories in 30 minutes, compared to about 175 calories walking.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Step_Mill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stiff-Legged Barbell Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Grasp a bar using an prise en pronation (palms facing down). You may need some poignets wraps if using a significant amount of poids. 2. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and vos jambes spaced using a epaules width or narrower stance. The genoux should be slightly bent. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the genoux stationary, lower the barre to over the top of vos pieds by bending at the hips while keeping votre dos straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from le sol until you feel a stretch on the ischio-jambiers. Inhale as you perform this movement. 4. Start bringing your torse up straight again by extending your hips until you are back at the position de depart. Exhale as you perform this movement. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stiff-Legged_Barbell_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stiff-Legged Dumbbell Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Haltères', '1. Grasp a couple of halteres holding them by your side at arm''s length. 2. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse straight and vos jambes spaced using a epaules width or narrower stance. The genoux should be slightly bent. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the genoux stationary, lower the halteres to over the top of vos pieds by bending at the waist while keeping votre dos straight. Keep moving forward as if you were going to pick something from le sol until you feel a stretch on the ischio-jambiers. Exhale as you perform this movement 4. Start bringing your torse up straight again by extending your hips and waist until you are back at the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this movement. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stiff-Legged_Dumbbell_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stiff Leg Barbell Good Morning', 'Bas du dos', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck) across it. 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance. Keep your head up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. Position de depart. 4. Keeping vos jambes stationary, move your torse forward by bending at the hips while inhaling. Lower your torse until it is parallel with le sol. 5. Begin to raise the bar en expirant by elevating your torse back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stiff_Leg_Barbell_Good_Morning/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stomach Vacuum', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Tenez-vous debout avec vos pieds epaules width apart from each other. Place vos mains on your hips. Position de depart. 2. Now Lentement, inhale as much air as possible and then start to exhale as much as possible while bringing your stomach in as much as possible and hold this position. Try to visualize your navel touching your backbone. 3. One isometric contraction is around 20 seconds. During the 20 second hold, try to breathe normally. Then inhale and bring your stomach back to the position de depart. 4. Once you have practiced this exercise, try to perform this exercise for longer than 20 seconds. Conseil : You can work your way up to 40-60 seconds. 5. Repetez for the recommended amount of sets.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stomach_Vacuum/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight-Arm Dumbbell Pullover', 'Pectoraux', 'Haltères', '1. Place a halteres standing up on a flat banc. 2. Ensuring that the halteres stays securely placed at the top of the banc, lie perpendicular to the banc (torse across it as in forming a cross) with only your epaules lying on the surface. Hips should be below the banc and legs bent with feet firmly on le sol. The head will be off the banc as well. 3. Grasp the halteres with both hands and hold it straight over your poitrine bras tendus. Both palms should be pressing against the underside one of the sides of the halteres. Position de depart. Caution: Always ensure that the halteres used for this exercise is secure. Using a halteres with loose plates can result in the halteres falling apart and falling on your face. 4. While keeping vos bras straight, lower the poids Lentement, in an arc behind your head while breathing in until you feel a stretch on the poitrine. 5. At that point, bring the halteres back to the position de depart using the arc through which the poids was lowered and exhale as you perform this movement. 6. Hold the poids on the initial position for a second and Repetez the motion for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight-Arm_Dumbbell_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight-Arm Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. You will start by grabbing the wide bar from the top pulley of a pulldown machine and using a wider than epaules-width pronated (palms down) grip. Step backwards two feet or so. 2. Bend your torse forward at the waist by around 30-degrees with vos bras fully extended in front of you and a slight bend at the coudes. If vos bras are not fully extended then you need to step a bit more backwards until they are. Once vos bras are fully extended and your torse is slightly bent at the waist, tighten the lats and then you are ready to begin. 3. While keeping the arms straight, pull the bar down by contracting the lats until vos mains are next to the side of the cuisses. Expirez as you perform this step. 4. While keeping the arms straight, go back to the position de depart while breathing in. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight-Arm_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight Bar Bench Mid Rows', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Place a loaded barre on the end of a banc. Standing on the banc behind the bar, take a medium, pronated grip. Tenez-vous debout avec your hips back and poitrine up, maintaining a neutral spine. Position de depart. 2. Row the bar to your torse by retracting the omoplates and flexing the coudes. Use a controlled movement with no jerking. 3. Apres une pause, Lentement, return the bar to the position de depart, ensuring to go all the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight_Bar_Bench_Mid_Rows/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Straight Raises on Incline Bench', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Place a bar on the ground behind the head of an incline banc. 2. Lay on the banc face down. With a pronated grip, pick the barre up from le sol, keeping vos bras straight. Allow the bar to hang straight down. Position de depart. 3. To begin, raise the barre out in front of your head while keeping vos bras extended. 4. Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Straight_Raises_on_Incline_Bench/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Stride Jump Crossover', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Stand to the side of a box with your inside foot on top of it, close to the edge. 2. Begin by swinging the arms upward as you push through the top leg, jumping upward as high as possible. Attempt to drive the opposite genoux upward. 3. Land in the opposite position that you started, on the opposite side of the box. The foot that was initially on the box will now be on the ground, with the opposite foot now on the box. 4. Repetez le mouvement, crossing back over to the other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Stride_Jump_Crossover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sumo Deadlift', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the epaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the epaules, which in effect lengthens vos bras. 2. Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hips and genoux. 3. As the bar passes through the genoux, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your omoplates together. 4. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sumo Deadlift with Bands', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. To deadlift with short bands, simply loop them over the bar before you start, and step into them to set up. Ensure that they under the back half of your foot, directly where you are driving into le sol. 2. Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the epaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. 3. Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hips and genoux. 4. As the bar passes through the genoux, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your omoplates together. 5. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift_with_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Sumo Deadlift with Chains', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. You can attach the chains to the sleeves of the bar, or just drape the middle over the bar so there is a greater poids increase as you lift. Attempt to keep the ends of the chains away from the plates so you don''t hit them when you lower the poids. 2. Begin with a bar loaded on the ground. Approach the bar so that the bar intersects the middle of the feet. The feet should be set very wide, near the collars. Bend at the hips to grip the bar. The arms should be directly below the epaules, inside the legs, and you can use a pronated grip, a mixed grip, or hook grip. Relax the epaules, which in effect lengthens vos bras. 3. Take a breath, and then lower your hips, looking forward with your head with your poitrine up. Drive through le sol, spreading vos pieds apart, with your poids on the back half of vos pieds. Extend through the hips and genoux. 4. As the bar passes through the genoux, lean back and drive the hips into the bar, pulling your omoplates together. 5. Return the poids to the ground by bending at the hips and controlling the poids on the way down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Bas du dos, Milieu du dos, Quadriceps, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Sumo_Deadlift_with_Chains/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Superman', 'Bas du dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, lie straight and face down on le sol or exercise mat. vos bras should be fully extended in front of you. Position de depart. 2. Simultaneously raise vos bras, legs, and poitrine off of le sol and hold this contraction for 2 seconds. Conseil : Squeeze your lower back to get the best results from this exercise. Remember to exhale during this movement. Note: When holding the contracted position, you should look like superman when he is flying. 3. Lentement, begin to lower vos bras, legs and poitrine back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. prescribed in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Superman/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Supine Chest Throw', 'Triceps', 'Medecine ball', '1. This drill is great for poitrine passes when you lack a partner or a wall of sufficient strength. Lay on the ground on votre dos with your genoux bent. 2. Begin with the ball on your poitrine, held with both hands on the bottom. 3. Explode up, extending through the coudes to throw the ball directly above you as high as possible. 4. Catch the ball with both hands as it comes down.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Supine_Chest_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Supine One-Arm Overhead Throw', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Lay on the ground on votre dos with your genoux bent. Hold the ball with one hand, extending the arm fully behind your head. Position de depart. 2. Initiate le mouvement at the epaules, throwing the ball directly forward of you as you sit up, attempting to go for maximum distance. 3. The ball can be thrown to a partner or bounced off of a wall.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Supine_One-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Supine Two-Arm Overhead Throw', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Lay on the ground on votre dos with your genoux bent. 2. Hold the ball with both hands, extending the arms fully behind your head. Position de depart. 3. Initiate le mouvement at the epaules, throwing the ball directly forward of you as you sit up, attempting to go for maximum distance. 4. The ball can be thrown to a partner or bounced off of a wall.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Supine_Two-Arm_Overhead_Throw/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Fallout', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Adjust the straps so the handles are at an appropriate height, below waist level. 2. Begin standing and grasping the handles. Lean into the straps, moving to an incline push-up position. Position de depart. 3. Keeping vos bras straight, lean further into the suspension straps, bringing votre corps closer to the ground, allowing your epaules to extend, raising vos bras up and over your head. 4. Maintain a neutral spine and keep the rest of votre corps straight, your epaules being the only joints allowed to move. 5. Pause during the peak contraction, and then Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Bas du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Fallout/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Push-Up', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Anchor your suspension straps securely to the top of a rack or other object. 2. Leaning into the straps, take a handle in each hand and move into a push-up plank position. You should be as close to parallel to the ground as you can manage with vos bras fully extended, maintaining good posture. 3. Maintaining a straight, rigid torse, descend Lentement, by allowing the coudes to flex. 4. Continue until your coudes break 90 degrees, pausing before you extend to Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Push-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Reverse Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Secure a set of suspension straps with the handles hanging about a foot off of the ground. Move yourself into a pushup plank position facing away from the rack. 2. Place vos pieds into the handles. You should maintain a straight posture, not allowing the hips to sag. Position de depart. 3. Begin le mouvement by flexing the genoux and hips, drawing the genoux to your torse. As you do so, anteriorly tilt your pelvis, allowing your spine to flex. 4. At the top of the controlled motion, Revenez en position de depart.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Reverse_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Suspend your straps at around poitrine height. Take a handle in each hand and lean back. Keep votre corps erect and your head and poitrine up. vos bras should be fully extended. Position de depart. 2. Begin by flexing the coudes to initiate le mouvement. Protract your omoplates as you do so. 3. At the completion of the motion pause, and then Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Suspended Split Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Suspend your straps so the handles are 18-30 inches from le sol. 2. Facing away from the setup, place your rear foot into the handle behind you. Keep your head looking forward and your poitrine up, with your genoux slightly bent. Position de depart. 3. Descend by flexing the genoux and hips, lowering yourself to the ground. Keep your poids on the heel of your foot and maintain your posture throughout the exercise. 4. At the bottom of le mouvement, reverse the motion, extending through the hip and genoux to Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Suspended_Split_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Svend Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Autre', '1. Begin in a standing position. 2. Press two lightweight plates together with vos mains. Hold the plates together close to your poitrine to create an isometric contraction in your poitrine muscles. Your fingers should be pointed forward. Position de depart. 3. Squeeze the plates between your palms and extend vos bras directly out in front of you in a controlled motion. 4. Pause at the top of the motion, and then Lentement, Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras, Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Svend_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('T-Bar Row with Handle', 'Milieu du dos', 'Barre', '1. Position a bar into a landmine or in a corner to keep it from moving. Load an appropriate poids onto your end. 2. Stand over the bar, and position a Double D row handle around the bar next to the collar. Using your hips and legs, rise to a standing position. 3. Assume a wide stance with your hips back and your poitrine up. vos bras should be extended. Position de depart. 4. Pull the poids to your upper abdomen by retracting the omoplates and flexing the coudes. Do not jerk the poids or cheat during le mouvement. 5. Apres une pause, Revenez en position de depart.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/T-Bar_Row_with_Handle/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tate Press', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc plat with a halteres in each hand on top of your cuisses. The palms of your hand will be facing each other. 2. By using your cuisses to help you get the halteres up, clean the halteres one arm at a time so that you can hold them in front of you at epaules width. Note: when holding the halteres in front of you, make sure vos bras are wider than epaules width apart from each other using a pronated (palms forward) grip. Allow your coudes to point out. Position de depart. 3. Keeping the upper arms stationary, Lentement, move the halteres in and down in a semi circular motion until they touch the upper poitrine while inhaling. Keep full control of the halteres en permanence and do not move the upper arms nor rest the halteres on the poitrine. 4. As you Expirez, move the halteres up using your triceps and the same semi-circular motion but in reverse. Attempt to keep the halteres together as they move up. Lock vos bras in the contracted position, Maintenez 1 seconde and then start coming down again Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up. 5. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tate_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('The Straddle', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. Begin in a seated, upright position. Start by extending vos jambes in front of you in a V. 2. With vos mains on le sol, lean forward as far as possible. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Mollets. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/The_Straddle/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Thigh Abductor', 'Abducteurs', 'Machine', '1. To begin, sit down on the abductor machine and select a poids you are comfortable with. When vos jambes are positioned properly, grip the handles on each side. Your entire upper body (from the waist up) should be stationary. Position de depart. 2. Lentement, press against the machine with vos jambes to move them away from each other while exhaling. 3. Feel the contraction for a second and begin to move vos jambes back to the position de depart while breathing in. Note: Remember to keep your upper body stationary to prevent any injuries from occurring. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Thigh_Abductor/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Thigh Adductor', 'Adducteurs', 'Machine', '1. To begin, sit down on the adductor machine and select a poids you are comfortable with. When vos jambes are positioned properly on the leg pads of the machine, grip the handles on each side. Your entire upper body (from the waist up) should be stationary. Position de depart. 2. Lentement, press against the machine with vos jambes to move them towards each other while exhaling. 3. Feel the contraction for a second and begin to move vos jambes back to the position de depart while breathing in. Note: Remember to keep your upper body stationary and avoid fast jerking motions in order to prevent any injuries from occurring. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Thigh_Adductor/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tire Flip', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Begin by gripping the bottom of the tire on the tread, and position vos pieds back a bit. Your poitrine should be driving into the tire. 2. To lift the tire, extend through the hips, genoux, and ankles, driving into the tire and up. 3. As the tire reaches a 45 degree angle, step forward and drive a genoux into the tire. As you do so adjust your grip to the upper portion of the tire and push it forward as hard as possible to complete the turn. Repetez as necessary.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Pectoraux, Avant-bras, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Épaules, Trapèzes, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tire_Flip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Toe Touchers', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Allongez-vous au sol or an exercise mat with votre dos pressed against le sol. vos bras should be lying across your sides with the palms facing down. 2. vos jambes should be touching each other. Lentement, elevate vos jambes up in the air until they are almost perpendicular to le sol with a slight bend at the genoux. vos pieds should be parallel to le sol. 3. Move vos bras so that they are fully extended at a 45 degree angle from le sol. Position de depart. 4. While keeping your lower back pressed against le sol, Lentement, lift your torse and use vos mains to try and touch your toes. Remember to exhale while perform this part of the exercise. 5. Lentement, begin to lower your torse and arms back down to the position de depart while inhaling. Remember to keep vos bras straight out pointing towards your toes. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Toe_Touchers/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Torso Rotation', 'Abdominaux', 'Swiss ball', '1. Stand upright holding an exercise ball with both hands. Extend vos bras so the ball is straight out in front of you. Position de depart. 2. Rotate your torse to one side, keeping your eyes on the ball as you move. Now, rotate back to the opposite direction. Repetez for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Torso_Rotation/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Trail Running/Walking', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Running or hiking on trails will get the blood pumping and heart beating almost immediately. Make sure you have good shoes. While you use the muscles in your mollets and buttocks to pull yourself up a hill, the genoux, joints and ankles absorb the bulk of the pounding coming back down. Take smaller steps as you walk downhill, keep your genoux bent to reduce the impact and slow down to avoid falling. 2. A 150 lb person can burn over 200 calories for 30 minutes walking uphill, compared to 175 on a flat surface. If running the trail, a 150 lb person can burn well over 500 calories in 30 minutes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Trail_Running_Walking/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Trap Bar Deadlift', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. For this exercise load a trap bar, also known as a hex bar, to an appropriate poids resting on the ground. Stand in the center of the apparatus and grasp both handles. 2. Lower your hips, look forward with your head and keep your poitrine up. 3. Begin le mouvement by driving through the heels and extend your hips and genoux. Avoid rounding votre dos en permanence. 4. At the completion of le mouvement, lower the poids back to the ground under control.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Trap_Bar_Deadlift/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tricep Dumbbell Kickback', 'Triceps', 'Haltères', '1. Start with a halteres in each hand and your palms facing your torse. Keep votre dos straight with a slight bend in the genoux and bend forward at the waist. Your torse should be almost parallel to le sol. Make sure to keep your head up. Your upper arms should be close to your torse and parallel to le sol. Your forearms should be pointed towards le sol as you hold the poids. There should be a 90-degree angle formed between your forearm and upper arm. Position de depart. 2. Now, while keeping your upper arms stationary, exhale and use your triceps to lift the poids until the arm is fully extended. Focus on moving the forearm. 3. Apres une pause, at the top contraction, inhale and Lentement, lower the halteres back down to the position de depart. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tricep_Dumbbell_Kickback/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tricep Side Stretch', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Bring right arm across votre corps and over your left epaules, holding your coudes with your left hand, until you feel a stretch in your triceps. Then Repetez for your other arm.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tricep_Side_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Overhead Extension with Rope', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope to a low pulley. After selecting an appropriate poids, grasp the rope with both hands and face away from the cable. 2. Position vos mains behind your head with your coudes point straight up. Your coudes should start out flexed, and you can stagger your stance and lean gently away from the machine to create greater stability. Position de depart. 3. To perform le mouvement, extend through the coudes while keeping the upper arm in position, raising vos mains above your head. 4. Squeeze your triceps at the top of le mouvement, and Lentement, lower the poids back to the start position.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Overhead_Extension_with_Rope/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Pushdown', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a straight or angled bar to a high pulley and grab with an prise en pronation (palms facing down) at epaules width. 2. Standing upright with the torse straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to votre corps and perpendicular to le sol. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. Position de depart. 3. Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your cuisses and the arms are fully extended perpendicular to le sol. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torse and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement. 4. After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the bar Lentement, up to the starting point. Inspirez as you perform this step. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Pushdown - Rope Attachment', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a rope attachment to a high pulley and grab with a neutral grip (palms facing each other). 2. Standing upright with the torse straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to votre corps and perpendicular to le sol. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the rope with the palms facing each other. Position de depart. 3. Using the triceps, bring the rope down as you bring each side of the rope to the side of your cuisses. At the end of le mouvement the arms are fully extended and perpendicular to le sol. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torse and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement. 4. After holding for a second, at the contracted position, bring the rope Lentement, up to the starting point. Inspirez as you perform this step. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_Rope_Attachment/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Pushdown - V-Bar Attachment', 'Triceps', 'Poulie', '1. Attach a V-Bar to a high pulley and grab with an prise en pronation (palms facing down) at epaules width. 2. Standing upright with the torse straight and a very small inclination forward, bring the upper arms close to votre corps and perpendicular to le sol. The forearms should be pointing up towards the pulley as they hold the bar. The thumbs should be higher than the small finger. Position de depart. 3. Using the triceps, bring the bar down until it touches the front of your cuisses and the arms are fully extended perpendicular to le sol. The upper arms should always remain stationary next to your torse and only the forearms should move. Exhale as you perform this movement. 4. After a second hold at the contracted position, bring the V-Bar Lentement, up to the starting point. Inspirez as you perform this step. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Pushdown_-_V-Bar_Attachment/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Triceps Stretch', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. Reach your hand behind your head, grasp your coudes and gently pull. Hold for 10 to 20 seconds, then switch sides.', 'Muscles secondaires : Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Triceps_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Tuck Crunch', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. To begin, Allongez-vous au sol or an exercise mat with votre dos pressed against le sol. vos bras should be lying across your sides with the palms facing down. 2. vos jambes should be crossed by wrapping one ankle around the other. Lentement, elevate vos jambes up in the air until your cuisses are perpendicular to le sol with a slight bend at the genoux. Note: Your genoux and toes should be parallel to le sol as opposed to the cuisses. 3. Move vos bras from le sol and cross them so they are resting on your poitrine. Position de depart. 4. While keeping your lower back pressed against le sol, Lentement, lift your torse. Remember to exhale while perform this part of the exercise. 5. Lentement, begin to lower your torse back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Tuck_Crunch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Dumbbell Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a halteres with each arm and place the upper arms on top of the preacher banc or the incline banc. The halteres should be held at epaules length. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the halteres until your upper arm is extended and the biceps is fully stretched. 3. en expirant, use the biceps to curl the poids up until your biceps is entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules height. 4. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position and Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Dumbbell_Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Clean', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place two kettlebells between vos pieds. To get in the position de depart, push your butt back and look straight ahead. 2. Clean the kettlebells to your epaules by extending through the legs and hips as you raise the kettlebells towards your epaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so. 3. Lower the kettlebells back to the position de depart and Repetez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos, Trapèzes. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Clean/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Jerk', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your epaules. Clean the kettlebells to your epaules by extending through the legs and hips as you swing the kettlebells towards your epaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so, so that the palms face forward. Squat down a few inches and reverse the motion rapidly driving both kettlebells overhead. Immediately after the initial push, squat down again and get under the kettlebells. Once the kettlebells are locked out, stand upright to complete the exercise.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Quadriceps, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Jerk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Military Press', 'Épaules', 'Kettlebell', '1. Clean two kettlebells to your epaules. Clean the kettlebells to your epaules by extending through the legs and hips as you swing the kettlebells towards your epaules. Rotate your poignets as you do so, so that the palms face forward. 2. Press the kettlebells up and out. As the kettlebells pass your head, lean into the poids so that the kettlebells are racked behind your head. Make sure to contract your lats, butt, and stomach for added stability.', 'Muscles secondaires : Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Military_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Two-Arm Kettlebell Row', 'Milieu du dos', 'Kettlebell', '1. Place two kettlebells in front of vos pieds. Bend your genoux slightly and then push your butt out as much as possible as you bend over to get in the position de depart. 2. Grab both kettlebells and pull them to your stomach, retracting your omoplates and flexing the coudes. Keep votre dos straight. Lower and Repetez.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Two-Arm_Kettlebell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Underhand Cable Pulldowns', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Adjust the genoux pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar. 2. Grab the pull-down bar with the palms facing your torse (a supinated grip). Make sure that the hands are placed closer than the epaules width. 3. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. Position de depart. 4. As you Expirez, pull the bar down until it touches your upper poitrine by drawing the epaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the entierement contracte position and keep the coudes close to votre corps. The upper torse should remain stationary as your bring the bar to you and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar. 5. After a second on the contracted position, while breathing in, Lentement, bring the bar back to the position de depart when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. 6. Repetez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Underhand_Cable_Pulldowns/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upper Back-Leg Grab', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. While seated, bend forward to hug your cuisses from underneath with both arms. 2. Keep your genoux together and vos jambes extended out as you bring your poitrine down to your genoux. You can also stretch your middle back by pulling votre dos away from your genoux as your hugging them.', 'Muscles secondaires : Bas du dos, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upper_Back-Leg_Grab/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upper Back Stretch', 'Milieu du dos', 'Autre', '1. Clasp fingers together with your thumbs pointing down, round your epaules as you reach vos mains forward.', 'Muscles secondaires : Milieu du dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upper_Back_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upright Barbell Row', 'Épaules', 'Barre', '1. Grasp a barre with an prise en pronation that is slightly less than epaules width. The bar should be resting on the top of your cuisses with vos bras extended and a slight bend in your coudes. votre dos should also be straight. Position de depart. 2. Now exhale and use the sides of your epaules to lift the bar, raising your coudes up and to the side. Keep the bar close to votre corps as you raise it. Continue to lift the bar until it nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion, and should always be higher than your forearms. Remember to keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement. 3. Lower the bar back down Lentement, to the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Trapèzes. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upright_Barbell_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upright Cable Row', 'Trapèzes', 'Poulie', '1. Grasp a straight bar cable attachment that is attached to a low pulley with a pronated (palms facing your cuisses) grip that is slightly less than epaules width. The bar should be resting on top of your cuisses. vos bras should be extended with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos should be straight. Position de depart. 2. Use your side epaules to lift the cable bar en expirant. The bar should be close to the body as you move it up. Continue to lift it until it nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the bar, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement. 3. Lower the bar back down Lentement, to the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upright_Cable_Row/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upright Row - With Bands', 'Trapèzes', 'Élastique', '1. To begin, stand on an exercise band so that tension begins at arm''s length. Grasp the handles using a pronated (palms facing your cuisses) grip that is slightly less than epaules width. The handles should be resting on top of your cuisses. vos bras should be extended with a slight bend at the coudes and votre dos should be straight. Position de depart. 2. Use your side epaules to lift the handles en expirant. The handles should be close to the body as you move them up. Continue to lift the handles until they nearly touches your chin. Conseil : Your coudes should drive the motion. As you lift the handles, your coudes should always be higher than your forearms. Also, keep your torse stationary and pause for a second at the top of le mouvement. 3. Lower the handles back down Lentement, to the position de depart. Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upright_Row_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Upward Stretch', 'Épaules', 'Autre', '1. Extend both hands straight above your head, palms touching. 2. Lentement, push vos mains up and back, keeping votre dos straight.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Dos. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Upward_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('V-Bar Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a V-Bar attached to the top pulley. 2. Adjust the genoux pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar. 3. Grab the V-bar with the palms facing each other (a neutral grip). Stick your poitrine out and lean yourself back slightly (around 30-degrees) in order to better engage the lats. Position de depart. 4. Using your lats, pull the bar down as you squeeze your omoplates. Continue until your poitrine nearly touches the V-bar. Exhale as you execute this motion. Conseil : Keep the torse stationary throughout le mouvement. 5. After a second hold on the contracted position, Lentement, bring the bar back to the position de depart as you Inspirez. 6. Repetez for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/V-Bar_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('V-Bar Pullup', 'Dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. Start by placing the middle of the V-bar in the middle of the pull-up bar (assuming that the pull-up station you are using does not have neutral grip handles). The V-Bar handles will be facing down so that you can hang from the pull-up bar through the use of the handles. 2. Once you securely place the V-bar, take a hold of the bar from each side and hang from it. Stick your poitrine out and lean yourself back slightly in order to better engage the lats. Position de depart. 3. Using your lats, pull your torse up while leaning your head back slightly so that you do not hit yourself with the chin-up bar. Continue until your poitrine nearly touches the V-bar. Exhale as you execute this motion. 4. After a second hold on the contracted position, Lentement, lower votre corps back to the position de depart as you Inspirez. 5. Repetez for the prescribed number of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/V-Bar_Pullup/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Vertical Swing', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Haltères', '1. Allow the halteres to hang bras tendus between vos jambes, holding it with both hands. Keep votre dos straight and your head up. 2. Swing the halteres between vos jambes, flexing at the hips and bending the genoux slightly. 3. Powerfully reverse the motion by extending at the hips, genoux, and ankles to propel yourself upward, swinging the dumbell over your head. 4. As you land, absorb the impact through vos jambes and draw the halteres to your torse before the next repetition.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Quadriceps, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Vertical_Swing/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Walking, Treadmill', 'Quadriceps', 'Machine', '1. To begin, step onto the treadmill and select the desired option from the menu. Most treadmills have a manual setting, or you can select a program to run. Typically, you can enter your age and poids to estimate the amount of calories burned during exercise. Elevation can be adjusted to change the intensity of the workout. 2. Treadmills offer convenience, cardiovascular benefits, and usually have less impact than walking outside. When walking, you should move at a moderate to fast pace, not a leisurely one. Being an activity of lower intensity, walking doesn''t burn as many calories as some other activities, but still provides great benefit. A 150 lb person will burn about 175 calories walking 4 miles per hour for 30 minutes, compared to 450 calories running twice as fast. Maintain proper posture as you walk, and only hold onto the handles when necessary, such as when dismounting or checking your heart rate.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Walking_Treadmill/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Ball Hyperextension', 'Bas du dos', 'Swiss ball', '1. To begin, lie down on an exercise ball with your torse pressing against the ball and parallel to le sol. The ball of vos pieds should be pressed against le sol to help keep you balanced. Place a weighted plate under your chin or behind your neck. Position de depart. 2. Lentement, raise your torse up by bending at the waist and lower back. Remember to exhale during this movement. 3. Hold the contraction on your lower back for a second and lower your torse back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. prescribed in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Ball_Hyperextension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Ball Side Bend', 'Abdominaux', 'Swiss ball', '1. To begin, lie down on an exercise ball with your left side of the torse (waist, hips and epaules) pressed against the ball. 2. vos pieds should be on le sol while vos jambes are crossed and hanging from the ball. Hold a weighted plate with your right hand directly to the right side of your head. Conseil : Make sure the smooth side of the plate is resting against your head. 3. Place your left arm across your torse so that your palm is on your obliques. There should be a right angle between your left forearm and upper arm. Position de depart. 4. Raise the side of your torse up by laterally flexing at the waist while exhaling. 5. Hold the contraction for a second and Lentement, lower yourself back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite. 7. Switch sides and Repetez the exercise.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Ball_Side_Bend/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Bench Dip', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. For this exercise you will need to place a banc behind votre dos and another one in front of you. With the benches perpendicular to votre corps, hold on to one banc on its edge with the hands close to votre corps, separated at epaules width. vos bras should be fully extended. 2. The legs will be extended forward on top of the other banc. vos jambes should be parallel to le sol while your torse is to be perpendicular to le sol. Have your partner place the halteres on your lap. Note: This exercise is best performed with a partner as placing the poids on your lap can be challenging and cause injury without assistance. Position de depart. 3. Lentement, lower votre corps en inspirant by bending at the coudes until you lower yourself far enough to where there is an angle slightly smaller than 90 degrees between the upper arm and the forearm. Conseil : Keep the coudes as close as possible throughout le mouvement. Forearms should always be pointing down. 4. Using your triceps to bring your torse up again, lift yourself back to the position de depart while exhaling. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Bench_Dip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Crunches', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos pieds flat on the ground or resting on a banc with your genoux bent at a 90 degree angle. 2. Hold a poids to your poitrine, or you may hold it extended above your torse. Position de depart. 3. Now, exhale and Lentement, begin to roll your epaules off le sol. Your epaules should come up off le sol about 4 inches while your lower back remains on le sol. 4. At the top of le mouvement, flex your abdominals and hold for a brief pause. 5. Then inhale and Lentement, lower yourself back down to the position de depart.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Crunches/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Jump Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Position a lightly loaded barre across the back of your epaules. You could also use a weighted vest, sandbag, or other type of resistance for this exercise. 2. The poids should be light enough that it doesn''t slow you down significantly. vos pieds should be just outside of epaules width with your head and poitrine up. Position de depart. 3. Using a countermovement, squat partially down and immediately reverse your direction to explode off of the ground, extending through your hips, genoux, and ankles. Maintain good posture throughout the jump. 4. As you return to the ground, absorb the impact through vos jambes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Jump_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Pull Ups', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Attach a poids to a dip belt and secure it around your waist. Grab the pull-up bar with the palms of vos mains facing forward. For a prise moyenne, vos mains should be spaced at epaules width. Both arms should be extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip. 2. You''ll want to bring your torse back about 30 degrees while creating a curvature in your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. Position de depart. 3. Now, exhale and pull your torse up until your head is above vos mains. Concentrate on squeezing yourshoulder blades back and down as you reach the top contracted position. 4. After a brief moment at the top contracted position, inhale and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de depart with vos bras extended and your lats fully stretched.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Pull_Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Sissy Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing upright, with feet at epaules width and toes raised, use one hand to hold onto the beams of a squat rack and the opposite arm to hold a plate on top of your poitrine. Position de depart. 2. As you use one arm to hold yourself, bend at the genoux and Lentement, lower your torse toward the ground by bringing your pelvis and genoux forward. Inhale as you go down and stop when your upper and lower legs almost create a 90-degree angle. Hold the stretch position for a second. 3. After your one second hold, use your cuisses muscles to bring your torse back up to the position de depart. Exhale as you move up. 4. Repetez for the recommended amount of times.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Sissy_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Sit-Ups - With Bands', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Start out by strapping the bands around the base of the decline banc. Place the handles towards the inside of the decline banc so that when lying down, you can reach for both of them. 2. Position vos jambes through the decline machine until they are secured. Now reach for the exercise bands with both hands. Use a pronated (palms forward) grip to grasp the handles. Position them near your collar bone and rotate your poignets to a neutral grip (palms facing the torse). Note: vos bras should remain stationary throughout the exercise. Position de depart. 3. Move your torse upward until your upper body is perpendicular to le sol while exhaling. Hold the contraction for a second and lower your upper body back down to the position de depart while inhaling. 4. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Sit-Ups_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Start by positioning two flat benches epaules width apart from each other. Stand on top of them and wrap the weighted belt around your waist with the amount of poids you feel comfortable with. Make sure your toes are facing out. 2. Once you are standing straight up with the poids hanging in between vos jambes, position vos bras so that they are fully extended to the side of votre corps. Position de depart. 3. Begin by bending the genoux as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to le sol). Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genoux should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that are perpendicular to the front. If your genoux are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genoux and the exercise has been performed incorrectly. 4. Begin to move the body back up by pushing le sol of the flat banc with the ball of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de depart. Exhale as you perform this portion of the exercise. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Barbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a flat banc with feet firm on le sol. Using a wide, pronated (palms forward) grip that is around 3 inches away from epaules width (for each hand), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. The bar will be perpendicular to the torse and le sol. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your middle poitrine. 3. Apres une pause, bring the bar back to the position de depart as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a decline banc with the feet securely locked at the front of the banc. Using a wide, pronated (palms forward) grip that is around 3 inches away from epaules width (for each hand), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. The bar will be perpendicular to the torse and le sol. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your lower poitrine. 3. Apres une pause, bring the bar back to the position de depart as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up. 4. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Decline_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Pullover', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc decline with both legs securely locked in position. Reach for the barre behind the head using a pronated grip (palms facing out). Make sure to grab the barre wider than epaules width apart for this exercise. Lentement, lift the barre up from le sol by using vos bras. 2. When positioned properly, vos bras should be fully extended and perpendicular to le sol. Position de depart. 3. Begin by moving the barre back down in a semicircular motion as if you were going to place it on le sol, but instead, stop when the arms are parallel to le sol. Conseil : Keep the arms fully extended en permanence. le mouvement should only happen at the epaules joint. Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. 4. Now bring the barre up while exhaling until you are back at the position de depart. Remember to keep full control of the barre en permanence. 5. Repetez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program. 6. When finished with your set, Lentement, lower the barre back down until it is level with your head and release it.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Decline_Barbell_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Make sure that you adjust the genoux pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar. 2. Grab the bar with the palms facing forward using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a prise large, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance wider than epaules width. For a prise moyenne, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your epaules width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your epaules width. 3. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. Position de depart. 4. As you Expirez, bring the bar down until it touches your upper poitrine by drawing the epaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work except for holding the bar; therefore do not try to pull down the bar using the forearms. 5. After a second at the contracted position squeezing your omoplates together, Lentement, raise the bar back to the position de depart when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. Inhale during this portion of le mouvement. 6. Repetez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Pulldown Behind The Neck', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Make sure that you adjust the genoux pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar. 2. Grab the bar with the palms facing forward using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a prise large, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance wider than your epaules width. For a prise moyenne, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your epaules width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your epaules width. 3. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse and head forward. Think of an imaginary line from the center of the bar down to the back of your neck. Position de depart. 4. As you Expirez, bring the bar down until it touches the back of your neck by drawing the epaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work except for holding the bar; therefore do not try to pull down the bar using the forearms. 5. After a second on the contracted position squeezing your omoplates together, Lentement, raise the bar back to the position de depart when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. Inhale during this portion of le mouvement. 6. Repetez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Pulldown_Behind_The_Neck/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Rear Pull-Up', 'Dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the palms facing forward using a prise large. 2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar, bring your torse forward and head so that there is an imaginary line from the pull-up bar to the back of your neck. Position de depart. 3. Pull your torse up until the bar is near the back of your neck. To do this, draw the epaules and upper arms down and back while slightly leaning your head forward. Exhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar. 4. After a second on the contracted position, start to inhale and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de depart when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. 5. Repetez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Rear_Pull-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Standing Barbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding a barre at the wide outer handle. The palm of vos mains should be facing forward. The coudes should be close to the torse. Position de depart. 2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Conseil : Only the forearms should move. 3. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the bar is at epaules level. Maintenez 1 seconde and squeeze the biceps hard. 4. Lentement, begin to bring the bar back to position de depart as your Inspirez. 5. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Standing_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide Stance Barbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your epaules (slightly below the neck) across it. 2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a wider-than-epaules-width stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance, and also maintain a straight back. Position de depart. 4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genoux as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to le sol). Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genoux should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your genoux are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genoux and the exercise has been performed incorrectly. 5. Begin to raise the bar en expirant by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide_Stance_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide Stance Stiff Legs', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a barre loaded on le sol. Adopt a wide stance, and then bend at the hips to grab the bar. Your hips should be as far back as possible, and vos jambes nearly straight. Keep votre dos straight, and your head and poitrine up. Position de depart. 2. Begin le mouvement be engaging the hips, driving them forward as you allow the arms to hang straight. Continue until you are standing straight up, and then Lentement, return the poids to the position de depart. For successive reps, the poids need not touch le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide_Stance_Stiff_Legs/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wind Sprints', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Hang from a pull-up bar using a pronated grip. vos bras and legs should be extended. Position de depart. 2. Begin by quickly raising one genoux as high as you can. Do not swing votre corps or vos jambes. 3 3. Immediately reverse the motion, returning that leg to the position de depart. Simultaneously raise the opposite genoux as high as possible. 4. Continue alternating between legs until the set is complete.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wind_Sprints/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Windmills', 'Abducteurs', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos bras extended out to the sides and vos jambes straight. Position de depart. 2. Lift one leg and quickly cross it over votre corps, attempting to touch the ground near the opposite hand. 3. Revenez en position de depart, and Repetez with the opposite leg. Continue to alternate for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Windmills/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('World''s Greatest Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. This is a three-part stretch. Begin by lunging forward, with your front foot flat on the ground and on the toes of votre dos foot. With your genoux bent, squat down until your genoux is almost touching the ground. Keep your torse erect, and hold this position for 10-20 seconds. 2. Now, place the arm on the same side as your front leg on the ground, with the coudes next to the foot. Your other hand should be placed on the ground, parallel to your lead leg, to help support you during this portion of the stretch. 3. After 10-20 seconds, place vos mains on either side of your front foot. Raise the toes of the front foot off of the ground, and straighten your leg. You may need to reposition your rear leg to do so. Hold for 10-20 seconds, and then Repetez the entire sequence for the other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Worlds_Greatest_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wrist Circles', 'Avant-bras', 'Poids de corps', '1. Start by standing straight with vos pieds being epaules width apart from each other. Elevate vos bras to the side of you until they are fully extended and parallel to le sol at a height that is evenly aligned with your epaules. Conseil : Your torse and arms should form the letter "T: Your palms should be facing down. Position de depart. 2. Keeping your entire body stationary except for the poignets, begin to rotate both poignets forward in a circular motion. Conseil : Pretend that you are trying to draw circles by using vos mains as the brush. Breathe normally as you perform this exercise. 3. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wrist_Circles/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wrist Roller', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. To begin, stand straight up grabbing a poignets roller using a pronated grip (palms facing down). vos pieds should be epaules width apart. 2. Lentement, lift both arms until they are fully extended and parallel to le sol in front of you. Note: Make sure the rope is not wrapped around the roller. Your entire body should be stationary except for the forearms. Position de depart. 3. Rotate one poignets at a time in an upward motion to bring the poids up to the bar by rolling the rope around the roller. 4. Once the poids has reached the bar, Lentement, begin to lower the poids back down by rotating the poignets in a downward motion until the poids reaches the position de depart. 5. Repetez for the prescribed amount of repetitions in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wrist_Roller/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wrist Rotations with Straight Bar', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your palms facing down; hands spaced about epaules width. Position de depart. 2. Alternating between each of vos mains, perform le mouvement by extending the poignets as though you were rolling up a newspaper. Continue alternating back and forth until failure. 3. Reverse the motion by flexing the poignets, rolling the opposite direction. Continue the alternating motion until failure.', 'Niveau : Debutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wrist_Rotations_with_Straight_Bar/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Yoke Walk', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. The yoke is usually done with a yoke apparatus, but is sometimes seen with refrigerators or other heavy objects. 2. Begin by racking the apparatus across the back of the epaules. With your head looking forward and back arched, lift the yoke by driving through the heels. 3. Begin walking as quickly as possible using short, quick steps. You may hold the side posts of the yoke to help steady it and hold it in position. Continue for the given distance as fast as possible, usually 75-100 feet.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Yoke_Walk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Zercher Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. This exercise is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. The correct height should be anywhere above the waist but below the poitrine. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, lock vos mains together and place the bar on top of vos bras in between the forearm and upper arm. 2. Lift the bar up so that it is resting on top of your forearms. If you are holding the bar properly, it should look as if you have vos bras crossed but with a bar running across them. 3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a epaules width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep your head up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. Position de depart. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section). 4. Begin to lower the bar by bending the genoux as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallel to le sol). Inhale as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genoux should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendicular to the front. If your genoux are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genoux and the exercise has been performed incorrectly. 5. Begin to raise the bar en expirant by pushing le sol with the ball of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de depart. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avance.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Zercher_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Zottman Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright and a halteres in each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse. 2. Make sure the palms of the hands are facing each other. Position de depart. 3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Your poignets should rotate so that you have a supinated (palms up) grip. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules level. 4. Maintenez 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps. 5. Now during the contracted position, rotate your poignets until you now have a pronated (palms facing down) grip with the thumb at a higher position than the pinky. 6. Lentement, begin to bring the halteres back down using the pronated grip. 7. As the halteres close your cuisses, start rotating the poignets so that you go back to a neutral (palms facing votre corps) grip. 8. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Zottman_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Zottman Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a halteres in each hand and place your upper arms on top of the preacher banc or the incline banc. The halteres should be held at epaules height and the coudes should be flexed. Hold the halteres with the palms of vos mains facing down. Position de depart. 2. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the halteres keeping the palms down until your upper arm is extended and your biceps are fully stretched. 3. Now rotate your poignets once you are at the bottom of le mouvement so that the palms of the hands are facing up. 4. en expirant, use your biceps to curl the poids up until they are entierement contracte and the halteres are at epaules height. Again, remember that to ensure full contraction you need to bring that small finger higher than the thumb. 5. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position and rotate your poignets so that the palms are facing down again. 6. Repetez selon le nombre souhaite.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermediaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Zottman_Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
